1
00:00:00,534 --> 00:00:03,936
(The final story of the packing saga)

2
00:00:05,373 --> 00:00:07,140
Seriously, this is insane.

3
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:09,541
Have I lost my mind?

4
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:17,583
- I can't believe it.
- Let's give her a hug!

5
00:00:17,584 --> 00:00:20,653
- Give her a hug.
- Group hug.

6
00:00:20,654 --> 00:00:23,456
(So, why did they end up crying?)

7
00:00:24,925 --> 00:00:30,463
(Still dark in the early morning)

8
00:00:31,098 --> 00:00:33,900
The sun rises on the final day.

9
00:00:33,901 --> 00:00:34,901
(Their lodging in Cemoro Lawang)

10
00:00:36,103 --> 00:00:38,771
- Done. Let's go.
- Let's go.

11
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:40,139
The sunrise squad!

12
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:41,373
(They're up early.)

13
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:46,546
It's about 3:30 a.m.

14
00:00:47,114 --> 00:00:50,616
The sunrise squad is leaving
their lodging.

15
00:00:50,752 --> 00:00:51,618
Oopsy!

16
00:00:52,487 --> 00:00:54,654
I'm finally wearing our Woopsi Tee...

17
00:00:54,655 --> 00:00:56,222
even though they'll be covered soon...

18
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,324
- since it's so cold.
- It's really cold.

19
00:00:58,325 --> 00:00:59,692
That must be it.

20
00:01:00,162 --> 00:01:01,394
Good morning.

21
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:02,762
- Good morning.
- Hello. Good morning.

22
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:03,963
My name is Dori.

23
00:01:03,964 --> 00:01:05,131
- Dori.
- Dori.

24
00:01:05,132 --> 00:01:06,533
My name is Dori.

25
00:01:06,534 --> 00:01:08,534
I'm a local guide from Mount Bromo.

26
00:01:08,535 --> 00:01:09,502
Okay.

27
00:01:09,537 --> 00:01:12,472
We're going
on a Mount Bromo tour together.

28
00:01:12,473 --> 00:01:13,640
Perfect!

29
00:01:13,641 --> 00:01:16,342
- Are you ready?
- Yes, we're ready!

30
00:01:16,744 --> 00:01:18,444
- This is our Jeep.
- Okay.

31
00:01:19,346 --> 00:01:22,915
If you're ready, we can take off.

32
00:01:23,517 --> 00:01:24,650
Okay!

33
00:01:24,651 --> 00:01:27,353
(Getting in the Jeep)

34
00:01:28,322 --> 00:01:31,524
(Dori even got jackets for them.)

35
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,726
I feel warmer.

36
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:36,029
- Yes!
- Yes!

37
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:38,231
- Okay. Are you ready?
- Yes.

38
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:40,699
To the King Kong viewpoint.

39
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:44,637
- Let's go!
- Here we go!

40
00:01:45,706 --> 00:01:48,774
Another new experience.

41
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:50,409
Season Two has started.

42
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:52,244
(It was filmed under the supervision
of our safety guide.)

43
00:01:53,013 --> 00:01:54,214
Dori.

44
00:01:54,215 --> 00:01:56,082
How long does it take to get there?

45
00:01:56,083 --> 00:01:57,583
About 45 minutes.

46
00:01:58,652 --> 00:02:00,353
- It takes a while.
- With no traffic.

47
00:02:00,855 --> 00:02:02,422
- Are there a lot of people here?
- A lot of people.

48
00:02:02,423 --> 00:02:04,390
There are many tourists in this area.

49
00:02:04,391 --> 00:02:07,760
(It takes about 45 minutes to get
to the King Kong Hill Viewpoint.)

50
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:10,963
It starts getting light around 5 a.m.

51
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,998
And the sun comes up at 5:35 a.m.

52
00:02:12,999 --> 00:02:13,966
I see.

53
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:17,369
I hope we can see it with a sea of clouds.

54
00:02:18,038 --> 00:02:21,007
It's going to be so bumpy.

55
00:02:22,343 --> 00:02:23,977
It might start getting brighter
on the way.

56
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:26,379
What is this? We should hold on to this.

57
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,380
(The fun of riding in a Jeep)

58
00:02:27,381 --> 00:02:28,715
Are you all right?

59
00:02:29,783 --> 00:02:34,053
(The car rattles
as they leave the village.)

60
00:02:34,855 --> 00:02:36,856
I feel like it's going to be steep.

61
00:02:37,424 --> 00:02:39,392
(Grabbing)

62
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:41,794
We're going up.

63
00:02:44,298 --> 00:02:47,166
It's getting colder...

64
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,168
- the higher we go.
- It'll be even colder up there.

65
00:02:50,604 --> 00:02:52,805
We're getting really high up.

66
00:02:54,741 --> 00:02:56,377
(They keep driving higher up in the dark.)

67
00:02:56,378 --> 00:03:00,312
We're going up this steep mountain road.

68
00:03:01,615 --> 00:03:06,419
(Hitting the unpaved road)

69
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,187
It's so steep.

70
00:03:09,122 --> 00:03:09,988
My gosh!

71
00:03:10,824 --> 00:03:12,725
Harimu is gone.

72
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:16,429
(Harimu fell asleep.)

73
00:03:16,897 --> 00:03:19,632
(Gabee and Sian also fell asleep.)

74
00:03:20,134 --> 00:03:23,269
(While the other members are sleeping,)

75
00:03:23,805 --> 00:03:27,840
(the car is heading toward the viewpoint.)

76
00:03:28,909 --> 00:03:31,410
There are so many Jeeps.

77
00:03:32,179 --> 00:03:35,014
There are even more tourists
than I thought.

78
00:03:35,015 --> 00:03:36,816
(It's bustling with people.)

79
00:03:37,051 --> 00:03:38,651
We're almost there.

80
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,688
Okay. We're here.

81
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:44,723
(The car slowly pulls up.)

82
00:03:44,724 --> 00:03:45,724
We're here.

83
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:49,228
Thank you.

84
00:03:50,263 --> 00:03:52,531
There are cafes too.

85
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:54,935
(While waiting for the sunrise)

86
00:03:54,936 --> 00:03:56,002
It's nice.

87
00:03:56,804 --> 00:03:59,038
Is there a place with a heater?

88
00:03:59,873 --> 00:04:04,410
(A bunch of shops and stalls are
in the rest area.)

89
00:04:04,579 --> 00:04:06,946
There are more shops than I expected.

90
00:04:08,148 --> 00:04:11,217
- It's really busy here.
- I know.

91
00:04:11,218 --> 00:04:12,184
(It's early, but still crowded.)

92
00:04:12,185 --> 00:04:14,987
- I like the atmosphere here.
- Me too.

93
00:04:14,988 --> 00:04:18,158
They sell some patches.
I want to buy some.

94
00:04:18,159 --> 00:04:20,092
We can buy some on our way back.

95
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:21,494
(Calling dibs on some volcano souvenirs)

96
00:04:21,495 --> 00:04:24,330
We still have some time.
Do you want to have some tea?

97
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:26,132
Okay. That's perfect.

98
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:29,468
- That sounds great.
- We really do.

99
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:32,838
Hello. Good morning.

100
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:35,541
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

101
00:04:35,542 --> 00:04:36,542
Morning.

102
00:04:36,543 --> 00:04:39,178
You can have a seat here.

103
00:04:39,179 --> 00:04:40,546
Thank you.

104
00:04:40,547 --> 00:04:41,480
(Sitting by the brazier)

105
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:43,616
It's so warm. Briquette fire!

106
00:04:44,418 --> 00:04:47,319
We could grill some meat over it.

107
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:51,661
(A cup of tea in a warm place
on a cold day)

108
00:04:52,993 --> 00:04:54,560
Here it comes.

109
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:56,629
Yes, please.

110
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:58,330
Thank you.

111
00:04:58,331 --> 00:04:59,865
It looks good.

112
00:05:01,035 --> 00:05:02,201
It's really hot.

113
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,704
Oh, my!

114
00:05:06,874 --> 00:05:08,607
It smells a little like chocolate.

115
00:05:09,176 --> 00:05:11,443
It does smell like cacao.

116
00:05:11,444 --> 00:05:13,279
Is it cacao?

117
00:05:14,114 --> 00:05:15,347
I like this.

118
00:05:15,348 --> 00:05:20,152
(While the older members
are savoring the local tea,)

119
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:22,421
(the younger members are taking a selfie.)

120
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,258
(Slurping)

121
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:30,029
The warm tea feels so good in my stomach.

122
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:34,166
(Dori brought something over.)

123
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:37,803
- You need this for the next activity.
- Thank you.

124
00:05:37,804 --> 00:05:39,004
Thank you.

125
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:41,440
These flashlights come in handy
when you're walking around.

126
00:05:41,441 --> 00:05:42,874
Thank you.

127
00:05:43,477 --> 00:05:45,778
Where can I see the stars?

128
00:05:46,013 --> 00:05:48,313
We can see the stars...

129
00:05:48,314 --> 00:05:50,616
from the sunrise spot later too.

130
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:56,255
It might be a little cold,
but the stars looked good on the way here.

131
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:58,557
It'd be nice if we could see them...

132
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:00,392
- Right.
- after this tea.

133
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:04,063
Let's finish this, then head out in a bit.

134
00:06:04,064 --> 00:06:05,097
Okay.

135
00:06:05,619 --> 00:06:07,820
Let's go.

136
00:06:08,301 --> 00:06:09,268
Let's go.

137
00:06:10,436 --> 00:06:12,370
We'll walk for about ten minutes.

138
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:14,407
- Okay. Ten minutes.
- Ten minutes.

139
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,509
It's pretty close.

140
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:17,577
(Ten minutes to the viewpoint)

141
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:20,512
It's glowing down there.

142
00:06:20,782 --> 00:06:22,548
It's getting bright.

143
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,650
It's glowing red.

144
00:06:24,651 --> 00:06:28,020
(The sky is starting to glow orange.)

145
00:06:28,555 --> 00:06:29,989
The sun is coming up.

146
00:06:30,624 --> 00:06:33,092
This might be the prettiest sunrise
I've ever seen.

147
00:06:33,093 --> 00:06:34,093
Seriously.

148
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:37,596
I can barely see anything in front of me.

149
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:41,667
It's pitch-black.

150
00:06:42,203 --> 00:06:44,904
I can't see anything
beyond the flashlight.

151
00:06:44,905 --> 00:06:46,105
- I know.
- True.

152
00:06:46,106 --> 00:06:47,540
(The road is dark
with no sunlight or streetlights.)

153
00:06:49,042 --> 00:06:50,676
They're going up the stairs.

154
00:06:51,878 --> 00:06:52,911
It's...

155
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:53,912
(Coming up to a steep section)

156
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:55,581
The trail looks like this.

157
00:06:56,383 --> 00:06:57,416
Here we go again.

158
00:06:57,852 --> 00:07:01,120
If we're not going uphill,
it wouldn't be us.

159
00:07:01,922 --> 00:07:04,790
It might be slippery. Be careful.

160
00:07:04,791 --> 00:07:06,826
- Be careful.
- Okay.

161
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:08,493
It's slippery here for sure.

162
00:07:09,329 --> 00:07:11,196
Is this volcanic ash?

163
00:07:11,732 --> 00:07:13,632
Is that why it's so smooth?

164
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:14,666
(Slippery with volcanic ash and sand)

165
00:07:14,667 --> 00:07:15,734
Volcanic ash?

166
00:07:16,536 --> 00:07:19,304
Come up slowly and carefully.

167
00:07:19,305 --> 00:07:20,539
(Climbing cautiously)

168
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:24,277
- We should watch our left.
- Watch out.

169
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:28,046
It's a sheer drop next to us.

170
00:07:28,047 --> 00:07:29,881
(A steep drop)

171
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:33,185
They should've at least put up
some dim streetlights.

172
00:07:33,186 --> 00:07:34,653
I think it's because...

173
00:07:35,487 --> 00:07:37,989
this is supposed to be a spot
for stargazing,

174
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,392
they don't want it to be too bright.

175
00:07:42,863 --> 00:07:44,796
It's really steep.

176
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:46,899
(Making their way up
using just their flashlights)

177
00:07:48,234 --> 00:07:49,267
Oh, dear.

178
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:51,870
We've met some people climbing
on all fours.

179
00:07:52,739 --> 00:07:55,307
- It's dangerous.
- Let's take it slow.

180
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,043
I'm scared.

181
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:02,247
Gabee, be careful.

182
00:08:05,253 --> 00:08:07,254
If you're tired, you can stop.

183
00:08:07,255 --> 00:08:08,788
Okay.

184
00:08:09,589 --> 00:08:12,558
It's dangerous here,
so we shouldn't push it.

185
00:08:12,559 --> 00:08:13,792
(Taking a short break)

186
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,428
I really want to climb,

187
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:19,531
but I'm scared I'm going to slip.

188
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:21,900
I slipped a bit earlier.

189
00:08:22,302 --> 00:08:24,136
My hands got really sweaty.

190
00:08:24,137 --> 00:08:25,504
It might be dangerous.

191
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:27,740
This rail is a little slippery here.

192
00:08:28,808 --> 00:08:30,709
Harimu, you're okay with climbing, right?

193
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:32,711
- Yes. I think I'm okay.
- Are you okay, Harimu?

194
00:08:33,446 --> 00:08:35,614
I want to keep going too, but I'm scared.

195
00:08:37,317 --> 00:08:39,518
Shall we pair up, then?

196
00:08:40,053 --> 00:08:42,121
- We'll stay here, then.
- Okay.

197
00:08:42,722 --> 00:08:44,956
Shall we go see
how different it is up there?

198
00:08:44,957 --> 00:08:46,158
- Let's go check.
- Okay.

199
00:08:46,493 --> 00:08:47,960
- Let's go.
- If it's around the same,

200
00:08:47,961 --> 00:08:49,561
we'll come back down.

201
00:08:49,562 --> 00:08:51,830
- Let's do that. Let's go.
- Let's go.

202
00:08:51,831 --> 00:08:53,131
(Won Ji and Harimu are heading up
to the top.)

203
00:08:54,768 --> 00:08:56,502
I'm completely...

204
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,470
focused.

205
00:08:59,806 --> 00:09:03,208
We're not doing much,
but I'm getting out of breath.

206
00:09:03,408 --> 00:09:06,679
Maybe because we're so high up,
but I'm out of breath for sure.

207
00:09:08,148 --> 00:09:09,115
We're almost there.

208
00:09:09,116 --> 00:09:10,649
- Okay.
- Yes!

209
00:09:11,118 --> 00:09:13,252
In 30 seconds.

210
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:15,354
- Thirty seconds? Let's go.
- Thirty seconds?

211
00:09:15,355 --> 00:09:16,989
(We're almost there!)

212
00:09:17,392 --> 00:09:19,024
Here it is. I see a lot of people.

213
00:09:20,026 --> 00:09:21,893
It must be a good viewpoint.

214
00:09:22,295 --> 00:09:24,162
(Surprised)

215
00:09:24,565 --> 00:09:26,932
I'm loving this atmosphere.

216
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:29,168
Oh, up there?

217
00:09:29,169 --> 00:09:31,670
- Yes. Okay.
- How nice it is.

218
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:36,609
It's so beautiful.

219
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:39,979
(Waiting for the sunrise
with their own hopes)

220
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:41,914
It's going to be so beautiful.

221
00:09:43,116 --> 00:09:44,249
I'm excited.

222
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:50,823
(A popular tourist spot in Indonesia,
the King King Hill Viewpoint)

223
00:09:52,659 --> 00:09:54,660
That's a volcano.

224
00:09:55,996 --> 00:09:59,531
- Isn't that a sea of clouds?
- We can see a sea of clouds too!

225
00:09:59,532 --> 00:10:01,532
This is absolutely unreal.

226
00:10:02,257 --> 00:10:07,970
(A breathtaking sea of clouds
and volcanoes)

227
00:10:12,588 --> 00:10:15,427
- You can see the sunrise on the left,
- Yes?

228
00:10:15,428 --> 00:10:18,227
and Mount Bromo on the right.

229
00:10:18,301 --> 00:10:21,387
So we can see both from right here.

230
00:10:21,388 --> 00:10:23,900
The sunrise and Mount Bromo.

231
00:10:23,901 --> 00:10:25,254
I might actually cry.

232
00:10:25,255 --> 00:10:27,627
You can see it in the reflection.

233
00:10:27,628 --> 00:10:30,581
(A stunning sunrise and a mystical volcano
side by side)

234
00:10:30,654 --> 00:10:34,501
Was this the Year of the Fire
or something?

235
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:36,336
- Red Horse.
- The Year of the Red Horse.

236
00:10:36,721 --> 00:10:38,389
It fits the volcano so well.

237
00:10:39,089 --> 00:10:40,006
I love this.

238
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:41,608
Let's soak up the energy.

239
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:44,244
- I feel so recharged.
- Let's take it all in.

240
00:10:44,677 --> 00:10:47,413
Mr. Volcano, send us your energy!

241
00:10:48,177 --> 00:10:49,649
This side is gorgeous too.

242
00:10:50,349 --> 00:10:51,251
Totally.

243
00:10:51,252 --> 00:10:53,319
That's Malang City.

244
00:10:53,538 --> 00:10:54,921
- Malang?
- That's Malang.

245
00:10:55,032 --> 00:10:56,623
So that's Malang City.

246
00:10:56,624 --> 00:10:57,724
We were just there.

247
00:10:57,725 --> 00:10:59,058
- Yesterday, right?
- Yeah.

248
00:10:59,059 --> 00:11:00,160
(Malang, just beyond the mountains)

249
00:11:00,161 --> 00:11:02,395
You can see all of Malang from here.

250
00:11:03,196 --> 00:11:05,365
We have a full panoramic view.

251
00:11:05,833 --> 00:11:10,026
We were literally right over there
last night.

252
00:11:10,059 --> 00:11:13,473
That's the town we stayed in.

253
00:11:13,546 --> 00:11:15,508
- We stayed there.
- That's where you guys stayed.

254
00:11:15,509 --> 00:11:17,212
It was the last village, right.

255
00:11:17,232 --> 00:11:19,232
That's crazy.

256
00:11:19,812 --> 00:11:22,182
It's gotten so much brighter.

257
00:11:22,982 --> 00:11:24,484
The outlines are really showing up now.

258
00:11:24,485 --> 00:11:27,410
You can see the volcano in the sunlight.

259
00:11:28,523 --> 00:11:34,757
(The clouds roll back,
revealing the volcano.)

260
00:11:34,863 --> 00:11:37,757
That's the volcano, right?

261
00:11:37,770 --> 00:11:40,408
- See the highest peak over there?
- Yeah.

262
00:11:40,448 --> 00:11:41,768
That's Mount Semeru.

263
00:11:41,948 --> 00:11:43,102
- Semeru?
- Mount Semeru.

264
00:11:43,168 --> 00:11:44,204
And I think...

265
00:11:44,321 --> 00:11:46,372
you guys went there yesterday.

266
00:11:47,974 --> 00:11:49,576
The waterfall is near Semeru.

267
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:51,647
Yeah, we saw it!

268
00:11:51,648 --> 00:11:52,845
- Really?
- Yeah.

269
00:11:52,846 --> 00:11:56,073
(Mount Semeru,
seen near Tumpak Sewu Waterfall)

270
00:11:56,186 --> 00:11:58,685
And now you can spot Mount Bromo.

271
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:03,122
It's the smaller one with the smoke.

272
00:12:03,123 --> 00:12:05,291
- The smoke!
- I see it, right down there.

273
00:12:05,292 --> 00:12:08,919
(Smoke billows from Mount Bromo's crater.)

274
00:12:09,295 --> 00:12:14,732
See the one in front?
It's bigger than Mount Bromo.

275
00:12:14,915 --> 00:12:16,636
- That's Batok.
- Batok.

276
00:12:16,637 --> 00:12:19,444
That one's dormant, though.

277
00:12:19,731 --> 00:12:22,203
So Semeru is active, and so is Bromo.

278
00:12:22,204 --> 00:12:27,150
(Only active peaks emit smoke,
like Bromo and Semeru.)

279
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:31,958
I've seen plenty of mountains
and sunrises before,

280
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:35,019
- but a volcano hits totally different.
- It really does.

281
00:12:35,099 --> 00:12:36,556
The craziest part is...

282
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:39,592
this is my first time
ever seeing a volcano.

283
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:40,927
- Really?
- Yeah, really.

284
00:12:41,087 --> 00:12:42,195
My very first.

285
00:12:42,873 --> 00:12:44,080
You got lucky today.

286
00:12:44,081 --> 00:12:50,336
Not a single cloud blocking
the sunrise or the peaks.

287
00:12:50,974 --> 00:12:54,484
During the rainy season,

288
00:12:54,517 --> 00:12:57,410
if you're unlucky, you won't see a thing.

289
00:12:57,411 --> 00:13:00,013
Over there? Nothing at all?

290
00:13:00,014 --> 00:13:02,014
Zero visibility.

291
00:13:02,015 --> 00:13:05,394
Just a wall of white fog.

292
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:08,594
- We are so lucky!
- You guys hit the jackpot.

293
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:11,024
You can see the whole panorama today.

294
00:13:11,113 --> 00:13:13,626
The sun and the sea of clouds over there,

295
00:13:13,819 --> 00:13:17,552
the volcano rumbling over here,

296
00:13:17,553 --> 00:13:20,166
and the city behind us.

297
00:13:20,747 --> 00:13:22,669
What a way to start the day.

298
00:13:23,569 --> 00:13:26,706
- The yolk is about to burst!
- This is too much to take in.

299
00:13:28,817 --> 00:13:30,443
(Meanwhile,
Gabee and Sian stayed behind below.)

300
00:13:30,444 --> 00:13:31,511
What a bummer.

301
00:13:33,350 --> 00:13:36,349
Why does this feel like New Year's Day?

302
00:13:38,550 --> 00:13:43,182
(Dawn bathed in a warm glow)

303
00:13:44,802 --> 00:13:47,427
Did you say you'd never seen a sunrise?

304
00:13:48,208 --> 00:13:49,629
Or that you had?

305
00:13:50,242 --> 00:13:52,065
I don't think I've seen one
since I was a kid.

306
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,074
I go watch one every New Year's Day.

307
00:13:55,075 --> 00:13:56,302
You hike all the way up here for it?

308
00:13:56,703 --> 00:13:58,371
No, usually Jeongdongjin.

309
00:13:58,528 --> 00:14:02,041
I just find a good spot
and watch it every year.

310
00:14:02,542 --> 00:14:04,944
Every time I watch the sunrise,
I think to myself...

311
00:14:06,579 --> 00:14:08,060
You drag yourself out
at the crack of dawn,

312
00:14:08,061 --> 00:14:09,716
already dead tired,

313
00:14:09,717 --> 00:14:11,784
because you have to leave by 5 a.m.

314
00:14:12,028 --> 00:14:14,028
You wait and wait,
but the sun just won't show.

315
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:17,790
You start wondering,
"What if it doesn't rise this year?"

316
00:14:17,791 --> 00:14:20,026
People start grumbling
and leaving one by one.

317
00:14:20,805 --> 00:14:24,230
But out of all the sunrises
I've ever watched,

318
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:28,368
not once has the sun failed to come up.

319
00:14:29,001 --> 00:14:31,537
Every single time,
it gives me a fresh push.

320
00:14:32,198 --> 00:14:34,198
If you just hold on,
the sun is bound to rise.

321
00:14:35,808 --> 00:14:39,812
That's what keeps me going
at the start of every year.

322
00:14:39,813 --> 00:14:41,777
(Clouds or not, the sun always rises.)

323
00:14:42,837 --> 00:14:44,837
It makes you feel all warm inside.

324
00:14:50,408 --> 00:14:52,125
Why am I tearing up?

325
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:54,927
I think I'm just overly emotional today.

326
00:14:54,928 --> 00:14:56,201
Maybe you've been carrying a lot lately.

327
00:14:57,363 --> 00:14:59,332
Maybe things have been heavy.

328
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:02,502
Don't cry, Sian. You're okay.

329
00:15:02,503 --> 00:15:04,646
(Her raw emotions bring tears
to her eyes.)

330
00:15:04,986 --> 00:15:08,174
Remember that fortune teller in Thailand?

331
00:15:08,884 --> 00:15:11,944
Did they say I cry easily?

332
00:15:12,057 --> 00:15:14,617
- I think she said your moods swing a lot.
- Something like that.

333
00:15:16,449 --> 00:15:19,152
Let me tell you word for word.
She said you're "all over the place."

334
00:15:21,002 --> 00:15:22,655
Why am I always all over the place?

335
00:15:23,122 --> 00:15:24,056
It's okay.

336
00:15:24,824 --> 00:15:28,060
My chest tightened
the second I saw the sun.

337
00:15:28,861 --> 00:15:31,063
My heart feels full, yet warm.

338
00:15:31,064 --> 00:15:33,240
(A breathtaking dawn
that touched her heart)

339
00:15:33,826 --> 00:15:35,892
(The sky brightens
as they share their thoughts.)

340
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:37,893
It's unreal. Look at that view.

341
00:15:39,539 --> 00:15:40,940
This place is insane.

342
00:15:40,941 --> 00:15:43,109
Looking at that edge actually scares me...

343
00:15:43,125 --> 00:15:44,844
now that it's bright enough to see.

344
00:15:45,144 --> 00:15:47,144
- It feels like I could tumble right down.
- Look over there.

345
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:49,916
- This is wild.
- That's terrifying.

346
00:15:50,173 --> 00:15:51,447
How does a landscape like this even exist?

347
00:15:51,448 --> 00:15:55,493
A camera could never capture this.

348
00:15:55,773 --> 00:15:58,558
It's unbelievable. Pure awe.

349
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:04,297
- You can see everything so clearly now.
- It's gorgeous.

350
00:16:05,498 --> 00:16:09,035
- That is absolutely stunning.
- Wow.

351
00:16:09,277 --> 00:16:10,996
This doesn't feel real.

352
00:16:10,997 --> 00:16:13,072
This is 100 percent my vibe.

353
00:16:15,377 --> 00:16:20,051
(And today, the sun rises without fail.)

354
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,515
This is unreal.

355
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:25,151
This is incredible. I've never seen...

356
00:16:25,852 --> 00:16:28,221
nature feel so crisp and grand...

357
00:16:28,313 --> 00:16:31,591
with such overwhelming presence.
I don't even dare to challenge it.

358
00:16:33,073 --> 00:16:35,333
- This is amazing.
- I'm so thankful for this.

359
00:16:35,334 --> 00:16:37,096
I had no idea
mountains could be this good.

360
00:16:37,153 --> 00:16:39,532
Right? Isn't it crazy?

361
00:16:40,386 --> 00:16:43,493
- This is insanely good.
- The sun with all of this...

362
00:16:43,494 --> 00:16:45,972
It's just wild.

363
00:16:46,915 --> 00:16:48,161
Total eye candy.

364
00:16:48,175 --> 00:16:50,692
- I want to take photos over there.
- We have to get some shots.

365
00:16:50,693 --> 00:16:52,578
There are going to be
like 5,000 people, though.

366
00:16:52,789 --> 00:16:54,789
Still, you should get the shot.

367
00:16:55,715 --> 00:16:57,783
It's just so breathtaking.

368
00:16:57,784 --> 00:16:58,718
Isn't it pretty?

369
00:16:58,749 --> 00:17:00,219
Seriously.

370
00:17:00,909 --> 00:17:01,988
Director!

371
00:17:02,242 --> 00:17:03,456
Come over here.

372
00:17:04,022 --> 00:17:05,289
(Snap)

373
00:17:05,542 --> 00:17:07,960
Director, look at this view!

374
00:17:08,294 --> 00:17:09,695
You need to see this too.

375
00:17:10,805 --> 00:17:13,165
Put that camera down for a second.

376
00:17:13,678 --> 00:17:14,931
Just set it down.

377
00:17:14,932 --> 00:17:16,365
(Now is not the time to be working.)

378
00:17:16,565 --> 00:17:20,139
Smile! Big smile!

379
00:17:20,285 --> 00:17:21,307
Love it.

380
00:17:21,308 --> 00:17:23,591
(Taking great shots of the crew first)

381
00:17:23,851 --> 00:17:25,805
(Now it's my turn.)

382
00:17:25,845 --> 00:17:27,109
This is unreal.

383
00:17:27,110 --> 00:17:28,569
With the morning sun hitting just right...

384
00:17:28,570 --> 00:17:29,782
The hype is at max.

385
00:17:30,243 --> 00:17:33,185
The sunlight looks like a natural filter.

386
00:17:34,086 --> 00:17:35,923
Dori!

387
00:17:35,943 --> 00:17:37,723
When I say, "1, 2, 3,"

388
00:17:38,691 --> 00:17:40,642
look over here and do this pose.

389
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:42,929
(Won Ji wants to shoot
a short-form video together.)

390
00:17:42,997 --> 00:17:44,390
- Got it.
- Okay?

391
00:17:44,397 --> 00:17:46,438
Hold on, let me put this away first.

392
00:17:46,818 --> 00:17:47,756
Here we go.

393
00:17:47,757 --> 00:17:49,151
(Dori practices the pose.)

394
00:17:49,477 --> 00:17:51,367
(Ready)

395
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:53,841
- In 1, 2, 3.
- "Oops!"

396
00:17:53,842 --> 00:17:56,355
(Takes a deep breath)

397
00:17:56,722 --> 00:17:57,986
(Glances over)

398
00:17:58,678 --> 00:17:59,779
Okay.

399
00:18:00,406 --> 00:18:02,114
One, two, three!

400
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,485
Awesome.

401
00:18:06,853 --> 00:18:08,006
- Looks good, right?
- Gorgeous!

402
00:18:08,007 --> 00:18:11,157
- Now zoom in right here.
- Zoom all the way in.

403
00:18:11,158 --> 00:18:12,581
(Dori is loving every second too.)

404
00:18:12,774 --> 00:18:14,560
Should we head further up?

405
00:18:15,161 --> 00:18:16,596
Let's move up closer.

406
00:18:16,597 --> 00:18:18,010
(Heading closer to the volcano)

407
00:18:18,477 --> 00:18:20,683
(Taking it all in)

408
00:18:21,133 --> 00:18:23,803
I want to snap a photo
in running shades too.

409
00:18:23,804 --> 00:18:24,837
Totally.

410
00:18:24,838 --> 00:18:27,506
- This backdrop calls for running shades.
- Oh, absolutely.

411
00:18:27,507 --> 00:18:28,927
(Coveting that gorpcore aesthetic)

412
00:18:29,475 --> 00:18:32,645
- Running shades with a windbreaker.
- That's the one.

413
00:18:32,734 --> 00:18:33,981
(Full of envy)

414
00:18:34,347 --> 00:18:36,182
I'll do hands in pockets,
looking off at the hills.

415
00:18:36,183 --> 00:18:37,247
That'll do.

416
00:18:37,443 --> 00:18:38,150
Nice.

417
00:18:39,343 --> 00:18:40,820
Should I have put on a headband too?

418
00:18:44,924 --> 00:18:46,993
I want to ditch this layer for the photo.

419
00:18:46,994 --> 00:18:48,594
- Can you help me slip this off?
- Sure thing.

420
00:18:49,424 --> 00:18:50,730
I can't lose the fit battle.

421
00:18:53,457 --> 00:18:54,400
Alright.

422
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:58,524
(The Woopsi Tee finally makes
its grand appearance.)

423
00:18:59,010 --> 00:19:00,604
(Here to out-style
the mountain chic crowd,)

424
00:19:01,032 --> 00:19:03,157
This spot is perfect.

425
00:19:03,158 --> 00:19:04,301
I should take this on 0.5.

426
00:19:04,302 --> 00:19:05,572
(Bromo's very own Woopsi girl!)

427
00:19:05,573 --> 00:19:06,579
Ready!

428
00:19:06,939 --> 00:19:10,646
(The Woopsi girl,
burning hotter than the volcano)

429
00:19:11,099 --> 00:19:14,905
- Take one from this angle too.
- Got it, switching sides.

430
00:19:18,119 --> 00:19:19,191
Nice.

431
00:19:19,365 --> 00:19:20,960
Let's do a video.

432
00:19:25,389 --> 00:19:28,050
I finally get to wear the Woopsi Tee.

433
00:19:28,051 --> 00:19:30,369
I'm not cold at all. I'm burning up!

434
00:19:32,791 --> 00:19:34,564
Alright, your turn!

435
00:19:34,565 --> 00:19:36,175
(The Woopsi Tee's long-awaited debut)

436
00:19:36,176 --> 00:19:37,209
Looking so cool.

437
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:38,564
(Now it's Won Ji's turn.)

438
00:19:38,730 --> 00:19:40,613
What should my pose be? "Woopsi?"

439
00:19:41,577 --> 00:19:42,930
Cross your arms.

440
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:43,783
Arms crossed, got it.

441
00:19:43,924 --> 00:19:45,017
Nice.

442
00:19:45,951 --> 00:19:47,386
This is perfect.

443
00:19:48,251 --> 00:19:50,356
Hands in pockets,
staring into the distance.

444
00:19:50,618 --> 00:19:51,691
Love it.

445
00:19:52,845 --> 00:19:54,660
- How's it looking?
- Looks incredible!

446
00:19:54,661 --> 00:19:55,728
So effortless.

447
00:19:55,729 --> 00:19:57,162
(Chic and aloof)

448
00:19:58,036 --> 00:20:00,199
Wait, Gabee is video calling!

449
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,768
Let's answer Gabee's call.

450
00:20:04,238 --> 00:20:05,370
Gabee!

451
00:20:06,472 --> 00:20:08,106
Happy New Year!

452
00:20:09,742 --> 00:20:11,676
- Happy New Year!
- It's lagging.

453
00:20:11,945 --> 00:20:13,011
No signal.

454
00:20:13,012 --> 00:20:14,312
(New Year's greeting lost
due to bad reception)

455
00:20:14,313 --> 00:20:15,347
This is so frustrating.

456
00:20:16,916 --> 00:20:18,483
Reception is terrible up here.

457
00:20:18,484 --> 00:20:20,986
- It's basically 1G.
- What did she say on KakaoTalk?

458
00:20:21,621 --> 00:20:23,222
She texted, "I'm thinking of coming up."

459
00:20:23,223 --> 00:20:26,091
- Tell her it's gorgeous up here!
- "Come on up!"

460
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:28,226
"It's a quick climb."

461
00:20:29,328 --> 00:20:31,329
- They're telling us to come up.
- How did they say it is?

462
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:32,664
(Gabee, come join us! It's a quick climb.)

463
00:20:32,665 --> 00:20:33,898
She says it's a quick climb.

464
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,435
Let's give it a shot...

465
00:20:36,436 --> 00:20:39,171
and if it's too much,
we'll just come back down.

466
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:40,672
Excuse me.

467
00:20:41,174 --> 00:20:43,874
Seeing the sunrise gave me
a boost of courage.

468
00:20:44,977 --> 00:20:47,345
Might as well go for it while we're here.

469
00:20:48,881 --> 00:20:51,416
Getting back down is going to be
the real challenge.

470
00:20:51,417 --> 00:20:53,218
(The morning sun reveals
the steep incline.)

471
00:20:53,753 --> 00:20:54,653
(Staying low to scramble up)

472
00:20:54,654 --> 00:20:55,854
At least visibility is good now.

473
00:20:56,756 --> 00:20:58,890
It's still pretty scary, though.

474
00:20:59,525 --> 00:21:01,092
Gabee, take the path on the left!

475
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,262
- Hang on, give me a second.
- Maybe we should just turn back.

476
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,164
- I feel like I'm going to slip.
- Let's not push our luck.

477
00:21:06,799 --> 00:21:08,100
Better not to get greedy.

478
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:09,335
Getting down is going to be brutal.

479
00:21:09,336 --> 00:21:10,969
You're wearing slides too!

480
00:21:10,970 --> 00:21:12,804
Just watching you makes me nervous.

481
00:21:12,805 --> 00:21:15,573
(Gabee's brave attempt ends in defeat.)

482
00:21:15,574 --> 00:21:16,875
I'm giving up.

483
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:19,844
(Tearing up)

484
00:21:19,845 --> 00:21:21,279
I'm just so frustrated.

485
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,548
I really wanted to make it up there.

486
00:21:23,549 --> 00:21:24,882
Are you actually crying?

487
00:21:25,554 --> 00:21:27,285
I'm so annoyed with myself.

488
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:34,059
(She's really crying.)

489
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:35,727
She's really crying!

490
00:21:35,728 --> 00:21:37,062
(Tears of sheer frustration)

491
00:21:37,103 --> 00:21:40,004
I wanted to go up too!

492
00:21:40,470 --> 00:21:41,403
Gabee!

493
00:21:41,404 --> 00:21:42,224
(Sniffles)

494
00:21:43,936 --> 00:21:47,105
It just wasn't safe, Gabee.

495
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,875
I'm sorry for dragging you into this.

496
00:21:49,876 --> 00:21:50,876
Don't be silly!

497
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:52,998
Gabee, are you...

498
00:21:53,338 --> 00:21:54,670
- still terrified?
- Yes, I am.

499
00:21:55,749 --> 00:21:57,949
The ground down there is completely flat.

500
00:21:58,580 --> 00:22:01,352
Right now, you kind of look
like a sideways crab.

501
00:22:01,353 --> 00:22:02,253
I can't do this.

502
00:22:02,588 --> 00:22:04,088
Let's just head back down.

503
00:22:04,390 --> 00:22:06,689
I think we got our fill of the view.

504
00:22:06,690 --> 00:22:09,260
If only I'd worn real shoes...

505
00:22:09,261 --> 00:22:11,629
(Eyes swollen, letting out her regrets)

506
00:22:11,833 --> 00:22:13,565
Let's head down.

507
00:22:13,566 --> 00:22:15,000
(Heading back down
before the waterworks start again)

508
00:22:15,001 --> 00:22:16,001
Take it slow.

509
00:22:16,402 --> 00:22:20,572
(Set out for the peak,
only to turn back halfway.)

510
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:24,876
And back to square one.

511
00:22:24,944 --> 00:22:27,878
I hope Gabee's anxiety is gone now.

512
00:22:29,281 --> 00:22:32,383
Honestly, though, I'm proud of us...

513
00:22:32,651 --> 00:22:34,620
just for making it up this far.

514
00:22:34,621 --> 00:22:37,855
- Really?
- For me, even waking up this early...

515
00:22:38,692 --> 00:22:40,260
was like, "Wow, I actually woke up!"

516
00:22:40,261 --> 00:22:41,860
"Wow, I scrambled all the way up here!"

517
00:22:42,128 --> 00:22:44,963
I feel a real sense of accomplishment,
no matter how small it might be.

518
00:22:44,964 --> 00:22:46,298
(Sian cherishes even the small wins)

519
00:22:46,632 --> 00:22:50,102
I don't know why I always fixate
on what I couldn't do.

520
00:22:50,103 --> 00:22:52,070
Think about everything you've pulled off.

521
00:22:52,071 --> 00:22:53,404
Give yourself some credit.

522
00:22:54,307 --> 00:22:55,206
Seriously.

523
00:22:58,778 --> 00:23:00,445
Let's take some photos!

524
00:23:03,149 --> 00:23:05,283
(Still pouting)

525
00:23:05,985 --> 00:23:08,687
(Deeply hunched shoulders)

526
00:23:08,921 --> 00:23:10,321
This looks great, Gabee!

527
00:23:11,290 --> 00:23:14,359
Total conqueror-of-the-summit vibe!

528
00:23:15,261 --> 00:23:16,728
(Cracking a smile, thanks to Sian's hype)

529
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:18,530
You're the queen!

530
00:23:18,864 --> 00:23:19,797
You're my queen!

531
00:23:20,266 --> 00:23:22,100
My queen doesn't cry!

532
00:23:23,119 --> 00:23:24,145
No.

533
00:23:24,205 --> 00:23:25,633
Queens cry too, actually.

534
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,743
They just wipe their tears fast!

535
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:33,211
Just act like you conquered the summit.

536
00:23:34,947 --> 00:23:36,280
Wow, look at that view!

537
00:23:36,281 --> 00:23:39,016
(Wherever I stand is the top.)

538
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:43,839
Let's do a heart!

539
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,559
- Look at that!
- Such a honeymoon vibe.

540
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,626
You know how to pose!

541
00:23:48,627 --> 00:23:51,296
(Hashtag: Crybabies_of_King_Kong_Hill)

542
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:52,330
Love it!

543
00:23:52,531 --> 00:23:54,699
- This looks amazing.
- That needs to be my lock screen.

544
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,100
- This one came out great, too.
- Totally.

545
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:57,034
(Commemorative shots locked in)

546
00:23:58,137 --> 00:24:00,272
Doesn't it feel weird
that today's our last day?

547
00:24:00,273 --> 00:24:03,208
Yeah, it feels surreal.

548
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:06,144
The thought of saying goodbye
makes me so sad.

549
00:24:06,912 --> 00:24:08,079
Well.

550
00:24:08,428 --> 00:24:10,261
- You don't feel the same?
- I mean...

551
00:24:10,262 --> 00:24:11,080
(Grabbing)

552
00:24:11,081 --> 00:24:12,475
- I mean...
- Lee Sian.

553
00:24:12,476 --> 00:24:13,844
Listen to me.

554
00:24:13,930 --> 00:24:14,919
I'm just more excited...

555
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:18,389
for when we hang out back in Seoul!

556
00:24:19,358 --> 00:24:20,259
Oh, that was smooth.

557
00:24:20,260 --> 00:24:21,559
Your variety skills have leveled up
so much!

558
00:24:22,428 --> 00:24:25,496
Aren't you basically a variety pro now?

559
00:24:25,698 --> 00:24:26,697
It's only been two weeks!

560
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,634
- You are insanely good.
- I'm insanely good.

561
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:31,969
(Totally on the same wavelength)

562
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,370
Just you wait. I'll clean up real nice.

563
00:24:33,371 --> 00:24:35,573
- I know.
- In Seoul, I'm absolute fire.

564
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:38,610
(Suddenly, hot girl alert)

565
00:24:38,611 --> 00:24:39,711
Nobody was doubting you!

566
00:24:39,712 --> 00:24:40,745
I'm telling you, I'm gorgeous there.

567
00:24:40,746 --> 00:24:41,947
We all know!

568
00:24:41,948 --> 00:24:43,448
Oh, stop it.

569
00:24:44,750 --> 00:24:46,184
Thanks for sticking with me.

570
00:24:46,185 --> 00:24:48,253
- Oh, Gabee.
- If I were waiting here alone...

571
00:24:49,121 --> 00:24:50,154
Are you holding up okay?

572
00:24:50,693 --> 00:24:51,893
Looks like they're heading down now.

573
00:24:52,792 --> 00:24:53,791
Hey there!

574
00:24:54,426 --> 00:24:58,229
- Happy New Year!
- Nice to meet you again.

575
00:24:58,731 --> 00:24:59,898
Happy New Year!

576
00:24:59,899 --> 00:25:01,566
Did you guys have fun?

577
00:25:02,039 --> 00:25:03,735
- Yeah!
- How are you feeling?

578
00:25:04,136 --> 00:25:05,870
You guys worked so hard.

579
00:25:05,871 --> 00:25:07,809
It was so much fun!

580
00:25:07,810 --> 00:25:09,173
Harimu is thoroughly satisfied.

581
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:11,008
It was seriously incredible.

582
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:13,411
Honestly, the view isn't
even that different up there.

583
00:25:13,412 --> 00:25:15,079
Let's grab a photo right here.

584
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:16,714
I actually think it looks closer
from this angle.

585
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:21,986
(Group shot with the volcanic backdrop)

586
00:25:23,423 --> 00:25:26,090
- We were here!
- We were here!

587
00:25:26,091 --> 00:25:28,759
- Wish us luck!
- Goodbye.

588
00:25:29,362 --> 00:25:31,296
Let's head down.

589
00:25:31,564 --> 00:25:34,532
Careful, going down is way more dangerous!

590
00:25:35,501 --> 00:25:38,369
Can I check out the patches and stickers?

591
00:25:38,705 --> 00:25:40,773
- Yellow is way cuter, right?
- Totally.

592
00:25:40,774 --> 00:25:42,474
Can I get these two?

593
00:25:42,809 --> 00:25:44,342
Let's grab some magnets, too.

594
00:25:45,178 --> 00:25:47,545
I'm getting this charm.

595
00:25:47,747 --> 00:25:49,514
- It's on me!
- Thanks, Won Ji!

596
00:25:49,515 --> 00:25:50,826
(Won Ji treating the crew)

597
00:25:50,827 --> 00:25:52,047
Thank you, Ma'am.

598
00:25:52,117 --> 00:25:54,852
- Thank you.
- Thank you very much.

599
00:25:54,853 --> 00:25:56,187
(Swooping in to say hi)

600
00:25:57,873 --> 00:26:00,024
(Stocking up on souvenirs)

601
00:26:00,025 --> 00:26:01,192
Nice.

602
00:26:01,494 --> 00:26:03,495
That corn smells insane.

603
00:26:03,496 --> 00:26:05,663
- I have to get some.
- That smell is irresistible.

604
00:26:06,799 --> 00:26:08,300
(Steaming hot corn)

605
00:26:08,301 --> 00:26:10,435
- That's already delicious.
- How many do you want?

606
00:26:10,436 --> 00:26:12,070
- Three!
- My treat!

607
00:26:13,629 --> 00:26:16,300
She's treating us
since it's the last day today!

608
00:26:16,842 --> 00:26:18,209
Look at that butter.

609
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,877
He lines the whole cup with butter first.

610
00:26:19,878 --> 00:26:21,412
(After coating the inside of the cup
with butter,)

611
00:26:22,648 --> 00:26:24,616
(he pours in a hearty scoop of corn.)

612
00:26:24,617 --> 00:26:26,951
- That looks incredible.
- Definitely.

613
00:26:26,952 --> 00:26:29,087
Wait, isn't this basically
Korean corn cheese?

614
00:26:29,088 --> 00:26:30,722
(A massive mountain of cheese)

615
00:26:30,723 --> 00:26:32,090
It looks so good!

616
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,557
Look at that portion!

617
00:26:33,792 --> 00:26:35,025
Thank you.

618
00:26:35,728 --> 00:26:36,628
Careful, it's hot.

619
00:26:40,566 --> 00:26:43,001
Popping that lid off was the highlight.

620
00:26:43,002 --> 00:26:44,936
- Hmm!
- Good?

621
00:26:46,305 --> 00:26:47,538
Let's move!

622
00:26:47,539 --> 00:26:48,606
(Even the snacks are perfect today.)

623
00:26:48,607 --> 00:26:49,474
This is so good.

624
00:26:50,676 --> 00:26:52,176
Everyone's in pure bliss.

625
00:26:53,345 --> 00:26:54,278
Thank you.

626
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:55,913
It's delicious.

627
00:26:58,727 --> 00:26:59,784
This is it.

628
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:01,951
- Right?
- Yes.

629
00:27:01,952 --> 00:27:02,771
Hey!

630
00:27:02,772 --> 00:27:04,753
(The Jeep comes on time.)

631
00:27:05,038 --> 00:27:06,655
- Hop on in.
- Hello.

632
00:27:06,859 --> 00:27:07,959
Hello!

633
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:09,027
(Back to the hotel)

634
00:27:09,828 --> 00:27:14,131
(Winding along mountain roads)

635
00:27:14,867 --> 00:27:18,803
(Cruising through vast volcanic sands)

636
00:27:20,005 --> 00:27:23,574
(Back at the hotel)

637
00:27:24,077 --> 00:27:25,577
Get a quick nap in if you want.

638
00:27:25,578 --> 00:27:28,213
- Thank you so much! See you soon!
- See you.

639
00:27:28,214 --> 00:27:30,381
See you at 12:30!

640
00:27:30,984 --> 00:27:32,150
Thank you!

641
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:33,818
(Meetup set for 12:30 p.m.)

642
00:27:34,453 --> 00:27:36,587
- We finally made it back.
- See you later.

643
00:27:37,122 --> 00:27:39,857
The town looks so charming
in the daylight.

644
00:27:40,792 --> 00:27:42,559
(While the crew takes a breather...)

645
00:27:43,095 --> 00:27:46,898
(Afternoon sunlight bathes the village.)

646
00:27:48,101 --> 00:27:51,970
It's about 12:45 right now.

647
00:27:53,238 --> 00:27:55,573
Heading out for our final activity
of the day!

648
00:27:55,574 --> 00:27:57,074
This is the very last item
on our trip itinerary.

649
00:27:57,543 --> 00:27:59,277
We're going to Mount Bromo!

650
00:27:59,711 --> 00:28:02,613
- It's so bright out.
- Right? The sun is blazing.

651
00:28:03,282 --> 00:28:04,716
You could totally just wear
short sleeves right now.

652
00:28:04,717 --> 00:28:06,418
Hey there!

653
00:28:06,419 --> 00:28:08,353
- How's everyone doing?
- Doing great!

654
00:28:08,354 --> 00:28:09,554
- Awesome.
- Did you get some sleep?

655
00:28:09,756 --> 00:28:10,823
Did you get some good sleep?

656
00:28:10,824 --> 00:28:12,557
- Yes.
- We're good.

657
00:28:12,558 --> 00:28:13,958
- Feeling refreshed?
- Yeah!

658
00:28:13,959 --> 00:28:15,026
(Energy dialed up to 100)

659
00:28:15,561 --> 00:28:17,699
We're heading to the Bromo Crater now.

660
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:19,797
First, we'll take the jeep.

661
00:28:19,798 --> 00:28:23,101
Then we'll stop by a photo spot.

662
00:28:23,102 --> 00:28:25,037
After that,
we'll head to the parking area...

663
00:28:25,038 --> 00:28:27,972
and hike up to the mountain from there.

664
00:28:28,574 --> 00:28:30,208
From that point, you'll still have to...

665
00:28:30,609 --> 00:28:31,609
take the stairs all the way up.

666
00:28:31,610 --> 00:28:33,678
There are around 247 steps.

667
00:28:33,679 --> 00:28:34,845
Sounds good!

668
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:37,582
A mere 247 steps is a breeze.

669
00:28:37,917 --> 00:28:39,117
Easy peasy squeezy.

670
00:28:39,118 --> 00:28:41,185
(They've become seasoned hikers
over the past 11 days.)

671
00:28:41,186 --> 00:28:42,220
Ready to roll?

672
00:28:42,221 --> 00:28:43,021
- Yes!
- We're ready.

673
00:28:43,022 --> 00:28:45,552
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

674
00:28:45,586 --> 00:28:47,115
(Off to Mount Bromo!)

675
00:28:47,116 --> 00:28:49,104
(Today's plan: 1. Photo op)

676
00:28:49,105 --> 00:28:50,528
(2. Mount Bromo hike)

677
00:28:50,529 --> 00:28:51,529
Back into the jeep!

678
00:28:51,930 --> 00:28:54,431
- Wait, our jeep got an upgrade!
- Seems like it.

679
00:28:54,967 --> 00:28:56,367
(A roomier jeep)

680
00:28:56,368 --> 00:28:58,135
This is nice!

681
00:28:58,537 --> 00:28:59,370
(The interior is spotless.)

682
00:28:59,371 --> 00:29:00,505
Love this!

683
00:29:00,506 --> 00:29:02,874
The seat texture...
is that how you describe it?

684
00:29:02,875 --> 00:29:04,674
- The feel of the leather?
- What should I call it?

685
00:29:04,675 --> 00:29:06,311
The seats just feel way higher quality.

686
00:29:06,312 --> 00:29:08,145
Plus, the AC is blowing cool.

687
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,847
- So stable.
- It's perfect!

688
00:29:09,848 --> 00:29:11,348
- We all set?
- Yeah!

689
00:29:11,450 --> 00:29:12,617
Thank you so much!

690
00:29:14,486 --> 00:29:16,720
Our final destination...

691
00:29:17,055 --> 00:29:18,756
Mount Bromo.

692
00:29:19,691 --> 00:29:22,729
On our way to Mount Bromo!

693
00:29:22,730 --> 00:29:25,429
I feel like we're shooting
a music video right now.

694
00:29:26,565 --> 00:29:28,733
(Bromo, here we come!)

695
00:29:28,767 --> 00:29:30,501
- Let's roll!
- Let's roll!

696
00:29:30,502 --> 00:29:33,370
(First stop: Photo op)

697
00:29:35,541 --> 00:29:38,179
The sun is relentless here.

698
00:29:38,180 --> 00:29:40,445
You can literally feel the UV rays
cooking your skin.

699
00:29:40,813 --> 00:29:42,613
(The afternoon sun kicks into full gear.)

700
00:29:43,015 --> 00:29:43,982
It actually stings a bit.

701
00:29:44,496 --> 00:29:45,186
Sting!

702
00:29:45,187 --> 00:29:46,818
(Everyone switched into lighter outfits)

703
00:29:47,819 --> 00:29:49,286
We're heading toward the savanna now.

704
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:50,721
Savanna!

705
00:29:50,722 --> 00:29:52,790
We're also stopping at Teletubbies' Hills.

706
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,725
Teletubbies' Hills?

707
00:29:54,994 --> 00:29:57,061
We're cruising through the savanna.

708
00:29:57,930 --> 00:30:00,298
Wait, you know Teletubbies?

709
00:30:00,327 --> 00:30:02,327
- Teletubbies!
- Teletubbies?

710
00:30:02,567 --> 00:30:04,303
- Yes.
- Teletubbies!

711
00:30:04,394 --> 00:30:06,801
Oh, Teletubbies.

712
00:30:06,802 --> 00:30:11,982
It's called that because it
looks like the hill in Teletubbies.

713
00:30:13,222 --> 00:30:15,180
But it's not its real name.

714
00:30:16,735 --> 00:30:17,835
It's a nickname.

715
00:30:17,836 --> 00:30:20,652
- It's called Watangan.
- Watangan.

716
00:30:21,056 --> 00:30:22,020
Teletubby,

717
00:30:22,136 --> 00:30:23,789
Dipsy, Laa-laa,

718
00:30:23,836 --> 00:30:25,016
and Po.

719
00:30:26,136 --> 00:30:28,226
Why is she Teletubby?

720
00:30:28,363 --> 00:30:29,561
It should be Tinky Winky.

721
00:30:29,928 --> 00:30:31,928
I watched it when I was three,
so I don't remember.

722
00:30:32,186 --> 00:30:33,565
I watched it when I was really young.

723
00:30:33,613 --> 00:30:34,833
I don't remember watching it after that.

724
00:30:34,834 --> 00:30:36,834
I can't match the names to the characters.

725
00:30:36,886 --> 00:30:37,639
- Really?
- Really?

726
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:39,640
- Laa-laa is yellow?
- Yes.

727
00:30:39,966 --> 00:30:41,473
So you guys don't really know Teletubbies.

728
00:30:41,546 --> 00:30:44,009
Not really. I only remember watching it.

729
00:30:44,191 --> 00:30:46,178
Their keychains are popular again
these days.

730
00:30:46,179 --> 00:30:47,844
(The first episode aired
before they were even born.)

731
00:30:48,317 --> 00:30:51,016
(Taking the babies to the Teletubby hill.)

732
00:30:51,117 --> 00:30:53,018
It's taking a while.

733
00:30:54,195 --> 00:30:56,688
Now we are at the sea of sand.

734
00:30:56,842 --> 00:30:58,990
Sea of sand?

735
00:30:59,928 --> 00:31:01,435
(Where?)

736
00:31:01,489 --> 00:31:03,028
- Wow.
- Wow.

737
00:31:03,069 --> 00:31:05,501
Goodness, look at that.

738
00:31:05,502 --> 00:31:07,502
It's like a different planet.

739
00:31:07,575 --> 00:31:09,575
It's like Mars.

740
00:31:09,695 --> 00:31:11,103
- It really looks like Mars.
- Right.

741
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:14,306
Totally.

742
00:31:16,647 --> 00:31:18,193
(Entering the sea of sand
the volcano created.)

743
00:31:18,207 --> 00:31:20,479
I just want to run across this place.

744
00:31:24,364 --> 00:31:27,604
(A vast land stretching
as far as the eye can see.)

745
00:31:27,704 --> 00:31:31,022
Wow, it's huge.

746
00:31:31,756 --> 00:31:32,991
This looks fake. It's surreal.

747
00:31:33,156 --> 00:31:35,961
- It feels like we're on Mars.
- It feels surreal.

748
00:31:38,289 --> 00:31:40,389
I want to ride a horse across this place.

749
00:31:40,390 --> 00:31:42,868
(The car is covered
in the rugged, sandy wind.)

750
00:31:42,869 --> 00:31:44,803
I just want to run through here.

751
00:31:46,189 --> 00:31:47,305
This is so cool.

752
00:31:47,306 --> 00:31:49,822
(Racing across the volcanic ash plains)

753
00:31:49,823 --> 00:31:51,823
How is this place so big?

754
00:31:52,336 --> 00:31:53,378
It's amazing.

755
00:31:54,679 --> 00:31:56,248
It's like "Mad Max."

756
00:31:56,416 --> 00:31:57,416
Seriously.

757
00:31:57,983 --> 00:31:59,284
A motorbike!

758
00:31:59,285 --> 00:32:02,510
- That makes it more like "Mad Max!"
- Exactly.

759
00:32:02,511 --> 00:32:04,256
There are so many.

760
00:32:07,793 --> 00:32:09,961
These vibes are incredible.

761
00:32:10,211 --> 00:32:11,463
Peak vibes.

762
00:32:12,164 --> 00:32:14,199
"Mad Max" for max vibes!

763
00:32:17,164 --> 00:32:18,570
I think we're stopping here.

764
00:32:21,529 --> 00:32:23,015
I'm so excited!

765
00:32:23,016 --> 00:32:24,910
On a desolate planet.

766
00:32:29,002 --> 00:32:30,615
What in the world?

767
00:32:30,822 --> 00:32:33,251
What is all this?

768
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:36,406
(They step out of the car in awe.)

769
00:32:36,407 --> 00:32:37,889
This looks amazing.

770
00:32:41,132 --> 00:32:43,728
- Goodness.
- This is amazing.

771
00:32:44,763 --> 00:32:46,465
This is crazy.

772
00:32:47,513 --> 00:32:49,801
Wow, Dori. Incredible.

773
00:32:54,233 --> 00:32:57,242
(A green hill fills their gaze.)

774
00:32:57,243 --> 00:32:58,443
Is this even real?

775
00:32:58,913 --> 00:33:00,378
Have you ever been
to a place like this before?

776
00:33:00,379 --> 00:33:01,480
Never.

777
00:33:05,299 --> 00:33:08,553
The color is quite unique.

778
00:33:08,554 --> 00:33:10,622
- It's beautiful.
- So beautiful.

779
00:33:11,223 --> 00:33:16,528
You can take photos here
with the hill in the background.

780
00:33:17,112 --> 00:33:19,598
Over there, you can take photos
with the savanna behind you.

781
00:33:20,532 --> 00:33:21,800
I'm so excited.

782
00:33:24,029 --> 00:33:30,262
(A vast savanna stretches out
behind them.)

783
00:33:30,675 --> 00:33:33,324
(Heading a little closer)

784
00:33:33,555 --> 00:33:35,280
It's like I'm inside a painting.

785
00:33:35,442 --> 00:33:36,882
- So true.
- Right?

786
00:33:37,482 --> 00:33:39,164
Doesn't it feel like we're
inside a picture frame?

787
00:33:39,165 --> 00:33:39,918
Exactly.

788
00:33:40,402 --> 00:33:41,902
(Not without a proper pose)

789
00:33:42,968 --> 00:33:44,389
Flowers bloom on volcanoes too.

790
00:33:45,223 --> 00:33:47,859
- Flowers bloom even on volcanoes.
- Flowers bloom even on volcanoes.

791
00:33:47,860 --> 00:33:49,606
(Walking in a row through the wildflowers)

792
00:33:49,607 --> 00:33:51,283
Flowers will bloom for you too.

793
00:33:51,403 --> 00:33:52,464
I love that.

794
00:33:53,394 --> 00:33:56,634
(Arriving at Dori's
recommended photo spot)

795
00:33:57,067 --> 00:33:58,914
It really feels like I'm in a painting.

796
00:33:58,915 --> 00:34:00,805
- This is unbelievable.
- It's so beautiful.

797
00:34:01,974 --> 00:34:04,031
We basically entered a painting.

798
00:34:04,078 --> 00:34:06,244
The photos can't capture all of this.

799
00:34:08,313 --> 00:34:10,582
Give me a peace sign.

800
00:34:11,460 --> 00:34:12,684
Yes!

801
00:34:13,518 --> 00:34:15,920
Your outfit is perfect for this place.

802
00:34:16,033 --> 00:34:17,522
It works.

803
00:34:17,956 --> 00:34:20,158
There's a reason I didn't wear my dress.

804
00:34:20,613 --> 00:34:22,593
(Pretty and comfortable is best now.)

805
00:34:22,686 --> 00:34:24,762
She's coming back!

806
00:34:25,173 --> 00:34:26,531
(A celebratory twerk)

807
00:34:26,532 --> 00:34:27,599
I'm getting a cramp.

808
00:34:28,333 --> 00:34:29,568
- Your turn.
- You look so pretty.

809
00:34:29,628 --> 00:34:30,569
Next!

810
00:34:31,803 --> 00:34:32,804
This looks insane.

811
00:34:32,805 --> 00:34:34,072
(Let's go, Harimu.)

812
00:34:34,275 --> 00:34:36,275
Take it off! What are you waiting for?

813
00:34:36,276 --> 00:34:37,509
Take it off!

814
00:34:37,702 --> 00:34:38,995
If she takes it off...

815
00:34:39,175 --> 00:34:41,413
- Woopsi!
- Woopsi!

816
00:34:42,208 --> 00:34:44,015
The colors match.

817
00:34:44,016 --> 00:34:46,051
You're giving international girl vibes!

818
00:34:46,388 --> 00:34:48,153
Like that girl you were
jealous of at the waterfall.

819
00:34:49,415 --> 00:34:52,624
I was so jealous of them.

820
00:34:52,782 --> 00:34:54,359
Pose. Strike a pose.

821
00:34:56,195 --> 00:34:58,282
(I'm the queen now.)

822
00:34:59,008 --> 00:35:00,799
You're so pretty!

823
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:03,884
(Queen of the hill)

824
00:35:04,504 --> 00:35:06,758
(Proud elders)

825
00:35:07,818 --> 00:35:08,863
(Giggling)

826
00:35:08,864 --> 00:35:11,764
(Her posing skills are on another level.)

827
00:35:12,718 --> 00:35:15,702
(Will we ever get used to this?)

828
00:35:16,915 --> 00:35:21,616
(Her energy makes
every shot worth taking.)

829
00:35:22,189 --> 00:35:24,356
Welcome to my garden.

830
00:35:24,462 --> 00:35:25,833
(Excited)

831
00:35:27,787 --> 00:35:29,946
(I'm the queen of this area.)

832
00:35:29,947 --> 00:35:31,463
- Shall we go now?
- Yes.

833
00:35:32,707 --> 00:35:35,353
(Taking photos of the other members too)

834
00:35:35,527 --> 00:35:37,527
(Swish)

835
00:35:37,528 --> 00:35:38,903
Look at that back view!

836
00:35:38,904 --> 00:35:41,039
Mommy!

837
00:35:41,533 --> 00:35:43,842
I love it. It's so natural.

838
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:46,578
Hooray!

839
00:35:46,787 --> 00:35:49,740
(The introvert burning
through her social battery)

840
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:51,616
Okay.

841
00:35:51,847 --> 00:35:53,385
Teletubby hills!

842
00:35:53,594 --> 00:35:54,653
This is great.

843
00:35:55,420 --> 00:35:56,388
Come on!

844
00:35:57,738 --> 00:35:59,698
- Are you done here?
- Yes.

845
00:35:59,738 --> 00:36:02,927
If you're finished here, we can go
to the jeep and take more photos.

846
00:36:02,928 --> 00:36:04,665
Okay, let's go.

847
00:36:04,785 --> 00:36:07,758
Ready for another music video by the jeep?

848
00:36:07,759 --> 00:36:09,164
Yes, let's go!

849
00:36:09,165 --> 00:36:10,735
Yes! Let's do it!

850
00:36:11,206 --> 00:36:13,872
Can all of us go on top of it?

851
00:36:13,873 --> 00:36:15,732
- Is it possible?
- Yes, it is.

852
00:36:15,760 --> 00:36:18,141
- Let's all climb on it.
- Everyone's going up.

853
00:36:18,142 --> 00:36:20,939
(Second photo spot: Jeep roof)

854
00:36:21,159 --> 00:36:23,715
Can you hold this for a sec?

855
00:36:23,893 --> 00:36:26,985
- She's going up!
- Number one, Won Ji!

856
00:36:27,652 --> 00:36:30,889
- This is scarier than I thought.
- Nice!

857
00:36:31,885 --> 00:36:33,191
Look at those long legs.

858
00:36:33,311 --> 00:36:36,240
- Go, girl!
- This is great!

859
00:36:36,525 --> 00:36:38,132
This is nice.

860
00:36:38,133 --> 00:36:39,292
It's cooler up here.

861
00:36:39,293 --> 00:36:40,765
It's so nice, right?

862
00:36:40,939 --> 00:36:43,001
(And finally,
Harimu climbs onto the roof.)

863
00:36:43,002 --> 00:36:44,269
Okay!

864
00:36:44,806 --> 00:36:49,290
Two should sit in the front,
and two should stand.

865
00:36:51,244 --> 00:36:52,310
Okay.

866
00:36:52,311 --> 00:36:53,544
Yes, that's good.

867
00:36:54,244 --> 00:36:55,880
(Screaming)

868
00:36:57,370 --> 00:37:00,655
(Posing on top of the jeep)

869
00:37:01,168 --> 00:37:04,015
Move.

870
00:37:04,635 --> 00:37:06,728
(Moving)

871
00:37:07,901 --> 00:37:09,594
He's climbing up.

872
00:37:09,608 --> 00:37:10,895
The passion.

873
00:37:12,523 --> 00:37:13,998
Ready? One, two.

874
00:37:15,276 --> 00:37:19,450
(A stunning shot
with lush greenery all around)

875
00:37:19,983 --> 00:37:22,003
(Excited)

876
00:37:22,029 --> 00:37:25,643
- Abra-ca-Empty!
- Abra-ca-Empty!

877
00:37:25,696 --> 00:37:29,214
- Let it go! Let it all go!
- Let it go! Let it all go!

878
00:37:30,415 --> 00:37:31,449
Yes.

879
00:37:33,018 --> 00:37:35,220
- Okay!
- What an ending.

880
00:37:35,610 --> 00:37:36,788
Perfect!

881
00:37:37,804 --> 00:37:39,891
Thank you.

882
00:37:39,892 --> 00:37:40,957
(Very satisfied)

883
00:37:41,377 --> 00:37:42,894
You memorized the dance moves.

884
00:37:42,895 --> 00:37:44,423
I know. I didn't even know I did.

885
00:37:44,424 --> 00:37:46,164
Were you secretly practicing?

886
00:37:46,197 --> 00:37:49,234
I really know the moves now.
My body remembers it.

887
00:37:50,622 --> 00:37:51,437
Wow.

888
00:37:56,374 --> 00:37:59,003
(Back in the car)

889
00:38:00,090 --> 00:38:01,279
That's hot!

890
00:38:01,517 --> 00:38:02,480
Guys.

891
00:38:03,270 --> 00:38:06,217
I'm sorry if my English is not good.

892
00:38:06,257 --> 00:38:07,552
- Me too.
- You know what?

893
00:38:07,770 --> 00:38:09,020
I'm really nervous.

894
00:38:09,368 --> 00:38:10,388
Why?

895
00:38:10,474 --> 00:38:12,891
Because of the cameras.

896
00:38:13,701 --> 00:38:15,560
(The cameras made Dori nervous.)

897
00:38:15,561 --> 00:38:17,034
It's good enough.

898
00:38:17,081 --> 00:38:19,464
Dori, we love you!

899
00:38:19,820 --> 00:38:21,053
(Relieved)

900
00:38:21,054 --> 00:38:23,935
- You were nervous?
- We didn't know.

901
00:38:24,167 --> 00:38:26,477
- No problem. You're fine.
- You're angels.

902
00:38:27,254 --> 00:38:28,959
- May I close the door?
- Yes!

903
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:30,008
Thank you.

904
00:38:31,218 --> 00:38:33,218
I guess he wants to do well.

905
00:38:34,071 --> 00:38:36,071
You're really okay!

906
00:38:39,685 --> 00:38:41,419
- Okay, guys!
- Yes!

907
00:38:41,738 --> 00:38:44,255
Now we're going to the crater
of Mount Bromo.

908
00:38:44,256 --> 00:38:45,983
Crater!

909
00:38:45,984 --> 00:38:48,996
- Are you ready?
- Yes!

910
00:38:48,997 --> 00:38:52,597
Bromo!

911
00:38:52,598 --> 00:38:55,567
Bromo, wait for me!

912
00:38:55,838 --> 00:38:58,703
Off to the last of the four landscapes.

913
00:38:58,704 --> 00:39:00,197
Let's go.

914
00:39:00,198 --> 00:39:03,931
(Off to the last landscape!)

915
00:39:05,024 --> 00:39:09,514
(Heading to Mount Bromo, the grand finale)

916
00:39:10,590 --> 00:39:11,749
This is crazy.

917
00:39:12,597 --> 00:39:15,019
Unbelievable.

918
00:39:17,630 --> 00:39:18,849
This place looks awesome.

919
00:39:18,850 --> 00:39:22,256
(Crossing the vast volcanic ash plains)

920
00:39:23,103 --> 00:39:24,896
This place is really fascinating.

921
00:39:25,597 --> 00:39:27,465
How is it this vast?

922
00:39:28,132 --> 00:39:29,868
The Earth is full of wonders.

923
00:39:30,168 --> 00:39:33,371
We're on Earth,
but it doesn't feel like it.

924
00:39:34,221 --> 00:39:35,340
It's crazy.

925
00:39:37,088 --> 00:39:38,548
We're really here.

926
00:39:41,028 --> 00:39:46,241
(Arriving at Mount Bromo parking area)

927
00:39:49,141 --> 00:39:50,221
It's so cool that it has a road.

928
00:39:52,333 --> 00:39:54,993
Welcome to the Bromo parking area.

929
00:39:55,239 --> 00:39:56,628
Bromo parking area!

930
00:39:56,629 --> 00:39:57,896
- Wow.
- Wow.

931
00:39:57,926 --> 00:40:00,431
- Is that what we saw in the morning?
- I think so.

932
00:40:02,033 --> 00:40:04,501
You can see the volcano from here.

933
00:40:05,770 --> 00:40:08,673
(Mount Bromo and Mount Batok)

934
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:12,443
From here to those stairs,
we have to walk two and a half kilometers.

935
00:40:12,444 --> 00:40:14,878
- Can you see the stairs over there?
- Yes.

936
00:40:15,546 --> 00:40:17,680
(They must walk 2.5 kilometers
to the summit.)

937
00:40:17,681 --> 00:40:19,015
So that is how we go.

938
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:21,351
- I got it.
- Stairs over there.

939
00:40:21,352 --> 00:40:22,219
(Stair section)

940
00:40:23,171 --> 00:40:24,788
There are the stairs up.

941
00:40:24,789 --> 00:40:28,489
(Climbing 247 stairs to the summit)

942
00:40:28,490 --> 00:40:30,928
This is literally the Stairway to Heaven.

943
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:32,596
This is crazy.

944
00:40:32,964 --> 00:40:35,064
We're breaking our limits
every single day.

945
00:40:36,028 --> 00:40:37,308
I'll show you the route.

946
00:40:37,836 --> 00:40:39,170
Let's go.

947
00:40:39,171 --> 00:40:40,738
Dori, let's go.

948
00:40:40,972 --> 00:40:42,916
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

949
00:40:43,598 --> 00:40:45,676
- Our final climb.
- Dori, are you ready?

950
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:49,680
(Dori, are you nervous?)

951
00:40:49,681 --> 00:40:51,719
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

952
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:53,884
You got this, Dori.

953
00:40:53,885 --> 00:40:55,953
We can run to the top.

954
00:40:56,421 --> 00:40:59,089
Yes, I'll run!

955
00:40:59,246 --> 00:41:01,419
No. Slow, but smooth.

956
00:41:02,126 --> 00:41:04,204
(Dori firmly sets the pace for everyone.)

957
00:41:04,229 --> 00:41:05,230
Slowly.

958
00:41:05,231 --> 00:41:06,764
Don't step in poop.

959
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:11,102
(This was filmed
with prior permission and safety staff.)

960
00:41:11,703 --> 00:41:12,603
What's that?

961
00:41:15,039 --> 00:41:15,972
Are those flowers?

962
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:17,107
Oh, right.

963
00:41:17,108 --> 00:41:18,908
We need to buy this.

964
00:41:18,909 --> 00:41:20,044
(Vendors are selling flowers.)

965
00:41:20,045 --> 00:41:21,511
These are edelweiss flowers.

966
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:24,514
You buy flowers here,

967
00:41:24,515 --> 00:41:26,483
make a wish,

968
00:41:26,885 --> 00:41:31,721
and toss them into the crater at the top.

969
00:41:32,057 --> 00:41:33,724
So the flower is an offering.

970
00:41:33,725 --> 00:41:35,358
For example, you could say,

971
00:41:35,727 --> 00:41:38,896
"I want to be rich."

972
00:41:38,897 --> 00:41:41,131
"Please give me lots of money."

973
00:41:41,532 --> 00:41:45,035
(Greedy wishes are allowed too.)

974
00:41:45,036 --> 00:41:46,070
Then let's each get one.

975
00:41:46,071 --> 00:41:47,037
Do you want to buy it?

976
00:41:47,038 --> 00:41:48,171
Definitely.

977
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:50,041
Let's make one wish each,
and one together.

978
00:41:50,066 --> 00:41:50,984
- Great.
- Great.

979
00:41:51,009 --> 00:41:52,342
Five, please.

980
00:41:52,343 --> 00:41:53,477
- Five?
- Yes.

981
00:41:53,978 --> 00:41:55,145
This one is pretty too.

982
00:41:55,146 --> 00:41:56,148
- I like this.
- It's big.

983
00:41:56,149 --> 00:42:00,985
(They carefully choose
the prettiest flowers.)

984
00:42:00,986 --> 00:42:02,419
Isn't this one pretty too?

985
00:42:02,420 --> 00:42:04,121
- Looks good.
- This one for our group wish.

986
00:42:04,122 --> 00:42:05,623
(They choose the fullest flower.)

987
00:42:05,624 --> 00:42:06,788
It looks like broccoli.

988
00:42:07,526 --> 00:42:08,792
This one is pretty.

989
00:42:08,793 --> 00:42:10,794
What kind of flower is this?

990
00:42:10,795 --> 00:42:12,029
Edelweiss.

991
00:42:12,054 --> 00:42:16,209
(Java edelweiss,
which grows in high-altitude regions)

992
00:42:16,234 --> 00:42:17,534
How much for five?

993
00:42:18,836 --> 00:42:19,936
It's 250,000 rupiah.

994
00:42:19,938 --> 00:42:21,438
Two hundred fifty thousand? Okay.

995
00:42:21,973 --> 00:42:23,740
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

996
00:42:23,741 --> 00:42:26,209
(Day 11: spent 250,000 rupiah
on wish flowers)

997
00:42:27,412 --> 00:42:29,279
(Ready to climb the volcano)

998
00:42:29,280 --> 00:42:32,082
We are completely ready.

999
00:42:32,083 --> 00:42:34,017
Completely ready.

1000
00:42:34,386 --> 00:42:36,086
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1001
00:42:36,087 --> 00:42:39,456
- Our final climb.
- Our final climb.

1002
00:42:39,457 --> 00:42:43,093
- Bromo.
- Bromo.

1003
00:42:43,094 --> 00:42:45,061
Bromo!

1004
00:42:45,763 --> 00:42:47,297
Our final terrain.

1005
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:51,434
It's incredible. What a sight.

1006
00:42:51,435 --> 00:42:53,503
- It's amazing.
- Absolutely.

1007
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,806
It looks like another planet.

1008
00:42:57,077 --> 00:42:58,579
It really does.

1009
00:42:58,604 --> 00:43:02,011
(Crossing 2.5 kilometers of sandy plains,)

1010
00:43:03,748 --> 00:43:07,718
(passing through a valley
of volcanic ash,)

1011
00:43:08,886 --> 00:43:11,454
(they're finally approaching
today's destination.)

1012
00:43:11,455 --> 00:43:14,657
I feel like I've come to another planet.

1013
00:43:14,658 --> 00:43:16,659
- Another planet?
- Yes.

1014
00:43:16,660 --> 00:43:17,794
This is Planet Bromo.

1015
00:43:18,563 --> 00:43:20,631
He said it's Planet Bromo.

1016
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,902
(Dust is blowing up
from under their feet.)

1017
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,770
I think I'm sinking even more
because it's sand.

1018
00:43:27,771 --> 00:43:29,472
Yes, sand is hard to walk on.

1019
00:43:31,676 --> 00:43:32,843
We're getting closer.

1020
00:43:33,478 --> 00:43:34,478
Right.

1021
00:43:34,879 --> 00:43:37,380
Those stairs we can see
at the end are our goal, right?

1022
00:43:37,381 --> 00:43:38,481
Yes.

1023
00:43:38,783 --> 00:43:40,417
That looks like a cliff.

1024
00:43:40,718 --> 00:43:43,086
The slope looks incredibly steep.

1025
00:43:43,087 --> 00:43:43,953
And it's high.

1026
00:43:44,989 --> 00:43:47,290
I'm so curious
about what's inside the crater.

1027
00:43:48,203 --> 00:43:51,094
I want to see magma.

1028
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:52,595
Can we actually see it?

1029
00:43:52,930 --> 00:43:56,065
There is a crater,
but there isn't any magma or lava.

1030
00:43:57,001 --> 00:43:59,335
- Only smoke comes out.
- Only smoke.

1031
00:43:59,336 --> 00:44:03,139
But in the morning or at night,
when it's dark,

1032
00:44:03,574 --> 00:44:05,842
you can see something like fire.

1033
00:44:06,878 --> 00:44:09,012
There's a red color.

1034
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:12,349
(The volcano is still active today.)

1035
00:44:12,584 --> 00:44:15,218
Is all of this volcanic ash and not sand?

1036
00:44:16,254 --> 00:44:17,254
- Dori.
- Dori.

1037
00:44:17,855 --> 00:44:21,424
- Is this sand or volcanic ash?
- Or just dust?

1038
00:44:21,425 --> 00:44:22,392
It's sand.

1039
00:44:23,261 --> 00:44:25,162
- Why is the sand black?
- Just sand?

1040
00:44:25,163 --> 00:44:27,531
It's sand from Bromo.

1041
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:34,271
(Volcanic sand that spewed out
during eruptions)

1042
00:44:39,610 --> 00:44:41,344
- Oh, no.
- Her shoe...

1043
00:44:42,280 --> 00:44:43,213
Her shoe...

1044
00:44:43,881 --> 00:44:44,881
is dead.

1045
00:44:50,822 --> 00:44:52,188
So, how does it feel?

1046
00:44:53,524 --> 00:44:55,625
(Not much he can do
but check how she's feeling)

1047
00:44:55,626 --> 00:44:56,493
Barefoot.

1048
00:44:57,495 --> 00:44:59,596
- It's okay.
- Is sand getting in?

1049
00:44:59,831 --> 00:45:01,131
No sand is getting in. It's fine.

1050
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:04,100
It finally came apart.

1051
00:45:04,125 --> 00:45:06,671
(Approaching the volcano
in an even lower position)

1052
00:45:07,171 --> 00:45:08,271
Let's go.

1053
00:45:08,296 --> 00:45:11,809
(Arriving at the volcanic ash valley)

1054
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:14,811
I guess magma flowed down this way.

1055
00:45:15,513 --> 00:45:16,847
Is that why it looks like this?

1056
00:45:16,848 --> 00:45:18,825
(A landscape shaped
over thousands of years)

1057
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:21,784
This was all a path for magma,
so that's why it looks like this, right?

1058
00:45:21,953 --> 00:45:23,186
Amazing.

1059
00:45:23,921 --> 00:45:26,356
Walking along the path
the magma once took.

1060
00:45:26,724 --> 00:45:28,024
Magma.

1061
00:45:29,026 --> 00:45:33,096
(Volcanic sand blowing
as they head toward the crater)

1062
00:45:33,598 --> 00:45:36,466
Hey guys. Doesn't this look
like a dried-up river?

1063
00:45:37,635 --> 00:45:39,035
But this actually is a river.

1064
00:45:39,304 --> 00:45:40,504
- A river?
- A river?

1065
00:45:41,405 --> 00:45:46,677
(The path turns into a river
during heavy rainfall.)

1066
00:45:47,111 --> 00:45:49,046
- That would be amazing too.
- This is such a cool path.

1067
00:45:49,047 --> 00:45:51,482
So this becomes a river when it rains.

1068
00:45:52,183 --> 00:45:53,049
Look.

1069
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:56,642
- It's a face.
- A face!

1070
00:45:56,666 --> 00:45:58,187
(A carving into the hardened volcanic ash)

1071
00:45:58,188 --> 00:46:01,725
- It looks melted down.
- That's cool.

1072
00:46:01,993 --> 00:46:04,261
It looks like lava flowed down.

1073
00:46:04,262 --> 00:46:05,462
Right?

1074
00:46:05,796 --> 00:46:07,563
Art created by nature.

1075
00:46:07,999 --> 00:46:11,168
- Art created by nature.
- Art created by nature.

1076
00:46:11,169 --> 00:46:13,403
By the way, I want to ask you something.

1077
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:16,072
What is "annyeonghaseyo?"

1078
00:46:16,407 --> 00:46:17,807
- Annyeonghaseyo.
- Annyeonghaseyo.

1079
00:46:17,808 --> 00:46:18,842
It means "hi."

1080
00:46:18,843 --> 00:46:21,045
(Suddenly,
a Korean language class begins.)

1081
00:46:21,112 --> 00:46:23,947
Can you use it anytime?

1082
00:46:23,948 --> 00:46:26,650
- Yes.
- Even in the morning or afternoon?

1083
00:46:26,984 --> 00:46:28,251
Annyeonghaseyo.

1084
00:46:28,252 --> 00:46:29,819
Annyeong, Bromo.

1085
00:46:31,622 --> 00:46:32,689
Annyeong, Bromo.

1086
00:46:32,690 --> 00:46:35,558
You can say it
when you're saying goodbye too.

1087
00:46:35,559 --> 00:46:36,994
Annyeong, Bromo. Okay.

1088
00:46:39,664 --> 00:46:41,031
It's cool in the shade.

1089
00:46:41,165 --> 00:46:42,031
It's good.

1090
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:44,134
This is hard.

1091
00:46:45,102 --> 00:46:46,069
Pretty hard.

1092
00:46:46,336 --> 00:46:49,472
One of us is gradually falling behind.

1093
00:46:49,607 --> 00:46:50,507
Oh, no.

1094
00:46:50,841 --> 00:46:52,208
Look behind you.

1095
00:46:53,844 --> 00:46:54,811
We've come a long way.

1096
00:46:55,146 --> 00:46:57,581
I wonder how beautiful it'll be
when we get to the top.

1097
00:46:58,616 --> 00:47:00,450
- The scenery is beautiful.
- It's beautiful back there.

1098
00:47:00,518 --> 00:47:01,518
(Where they watched the sunrise)

1099
00:47:01,519 --> 00:47:03,620
(The view along the path they've walked)

1100
00:47:03,621 --> 00:47:05,622
My legs are working hard.

1101
00:47:05,724 --> 00:47:07,957
My muscles are pumping up.

1102
00:47:07,958 --> 00:47:09,025
Let's work out.

1103
00:47:09,927 --> 00:47:11,628
I'm stronger now.

1104
00:47:12,363 --> 00:47:13,530
Not bad.

1105
00:47:14,165 --> 00:47:15,665
We're surrounded by rocks.

1106
00:47:18,102 --> 00:47:20,370
It almost looks like
the mud stopped flowing.

1107
00:47:20,371 --> 00:47:21,304
Exactly.

1108
00:47:22,039 --> 00:47:23,373
- Right.
- Right.

1109
00:47:23,774 --> 00:47:24,874
It's fascinating.

1110
00:47:26,244 --> 00:47:28,779
I've always wanted to go
to the Grand Canyon.

1111
00:47:28,780 --> 00:47:31,515
This kind of feels similar.

1112
00:47:32,883 --> 00:47:35,484
(Amazed)

1113
00:47:36,120 --> 00:47:39,189
Heave-ho.

1114
00:47:40,625 --> 00:47:42,058
We've come a long way, right?

1115
00:47:42,994 --> 00:47:44,561
We have.

1116
00:47:46,797 --> 00:47:48,698
- I can see the stairs now.
- Really?

1117
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:51,000
Hang in there a little longer.
We're almost there.

1118
00:47:52,103 --> 00:47:54,304
I can see the people at the top now too.

1119
00:47:54,305 --> 00:47:56,140
- It feels like we're getting close.
- Yes.

1120
00:47:56,141 --> 00:47:57,707
It's not as bad as I thought.

1121
00:47:57,708 --> 00:47:58,809
(The summit finally comes into view.)

1122
00:47:58,810 --> 00:47:59,910
I love this.

1123
00:48:00,045 --> 00:48:01,911
The stairs aren't that long.

1124
00:48:01,912 --> 00:48:03,414
- Right.
- It's 250 steps.

1125
00:48:03,415 --> 00:48:06,049
Honestly, getting here felt much longer.

1126
00:48:06,050 --> 00:48:06,983
(Nearing the final hurdle)

1127
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:09,451
The mountain that swallowed the sun.

1128
00:48:09,620 --> 00:48:11,756
We saw it from far away,
and now we're here.

1129
00:48:11,777 --> 00:48:13,257
- Look over there.
- It's beautiful.

1130
00:48:13,924 --> 00:48:15,825
The sun is hanging right in the middle.

1131
00:48:16,129 --> 00:48:17,627
It's wearing a sun hat.

1132
00:48:17,628 --> 00:48:19,496
It's so cute. It looks like a little hat.

1133
00:48:19,497 --> 00:48:21,364
Our hats look like that too.

1134
00:48:21,365 --> 00:48:22,365
I know.

1135
00:48:23,501 --> 00:48:25,135
Did they get the idea from that?

1136
00:48:25,136 --> 00:48:26,670
Maybe they were inspired by it.

1137
00:48:27,371 --> 00:48:28,404
We're almost there.

1138
00:48:30,040 --> 00:48:32,542
- You can rest there for a bit.
- Okay.

1139
00:48:33,811 --> 00:48:35,845
This place is totally a desert.

1140
00:48:35,846 --> 00:48:37,414
(The final resting point
before the crater)

1141
00:48:38,181 --> 00:48:40,283
I can feel sand crunching in my mouth.

1142
00:48:40,284 --> 00:48:43,252
- I know.
- This really does feel like a desert.

1143
00:48:43,253 --> 00:48:46,536
They said there were
four types of terrain, but honestly,

1144
00:48:46,537 --> 00:48:48,591
I feel like we've been through ten.

1145
00:48:48,592 --> 00:48:50,826
Ten types of terrain and twenty mountains.

1146
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:54,031
But each mountain has
slightly different features.

1147
00:48:54,032 --> 00:48:56,166
A cave mountain, a waterfall mountain,

1148
00:48:56,534 --> 00:48:57,567
and a volcano.

1149
00:48:59,237 --> 00:49:02,205
You know that educational TV show
about famous mountains?

1150
00:49:02,873 --> 00:49:04,674
Like the famous mountains of the world.

1151
00:49:04,675 --> 00:49:07,043
(Somehow...)

1152
00:49:08,546 --> 00:49:09,546
Amazing.

1153
00:49:12,183 --> 00:49:13,850
We walked all the way from over there.

1154
00:49:13,851 --> 00:49:14,851
It's incredible.

1155
00:49:15,686 --> 00:49:16,753
Where's our jeep?

1156
00:49:17,488 --> 00:49:19,222
- There.
- The last one.

1157
00:49:19,930 --> 00:49:24,261
(The car and the people look
so tiny from here.)

1158
00:49:24,395 --> 00:49:26,629
Orange, blue, blue...

1159
00:49:27,033 --> 00:49:29,732
Your eyesight is seriously amazing.

1160
00:49:29,934 --> 00:49:30,834
I'm a camel.

1161
00:49:30,835 --> 00:49:32,002
(Longer eyelashes, better eyesight)

1162
00:49:32,003 --> 00:49:33,703
Mongolian eyesight.

1163
00:49:36,340 --> 00:49:37,440
This feels so rewarding.

1164
00:49:39,677 --> 00:49:41,678
- Let's go.
- We rested for quite a while.

1165
00:49:41,703 --> 00:49:45,315
(Setting off for the crater again)

1166
00:49:45,950 --> 00:49:47,215
We're finally climbing up here.

1167
00:49:48,986 --> 00:49:52,889
- It's been a while, Mr. Elephant.
- It's been a while.

1168
00:49:52,890 --> 00:49:57,126
This is the elephant god, Ganesha.

1169
00:49:57,127 --> 00:50:00,028
(Ganesha statue,
a Hindu deity symbolizing wisdom)

1170
00:50:00,029 --> 00:50:01,664
- You know that?
- I've heard about that.

1171
00:50:01,803 --> 00:50:03,937
It's a god of luck.

1172
00:50:04,541 --> 00:50:05,976
- A god of luck.
- A god of luck.

1173
00:50:06,957 --> 00:50:10,061
(She's already making a wish.)

1174
00:50:10,395 --> 00:50:14,028
We'll make a wish to Ganesha
and throw flowers.

1175
00:50:14,055 --> 00:50:16,019
- Okay. I got it.
- All right.

1176
00:50:16,035 --> 00:50:16,853
Let's go.

1177
00:50:16,854 --> 00:50:18,188
Actions speak louder than words.

1178
00:50:19,241 --> 00:50:21,157
- I like that.
- Actions over words.

1179
00:50:21,933 --> 00:50:23,527
There are the stairs.

1180
00:50:23,793 --> 00:50:26,029
It looks like an escalator.

1181
00:50:26,530 --> 00:50:28,698
It's really well-made.

1182
00:50:29,833 --> 00:50:32,903
We're almost there.

1183
00:50:34,570 --> 00:50:35,472
We can do this.

1184
00:50:35,624 --> 00:50:37,274
Yes! We can do this!

1185
00:50:37,997 --> 00:50:39,709
You're okay.

1186
00:50:40,804 --> 00:50:45,295
(As Gabee gets close to the stairs,
she looks more serious.)

1187
00:50:46,022 --> 00:50:50,028
(For safety,
the production team goes first.)

1188
00:50:50,448 --> 00:50:53,890
Be careful. You might fall.

1189
00:50:56,740 --> 00:50:59,693
(Staring)

1190
00:51:00,633 --> 00:51:04,679
(Just looking at the stairs
makes you dizzy.)

1191
00:51:05,919 --> 00:51:10,313
(There are 247 steps ahead of them.)

1192
00:51:12,204 --> 00:51:13,243
My goodness.

1193
00:51:15,352 --> 00:51:16,713
I feel like a coward.

1194
00:51:18,982 --> 00:51:20,982
One slip and it's over.

1195
00:51:22,953 --> 00:51:24,875
That was terrifying.

1196
00:51:24,876 --> 00:51:28,555
(Gabee suddenly feels scared.)

1197
00:51:29,355 --> 00:51:33,322
(They have to be extra careful
since the stairs are covered in sand.)

1198
00:51:34,042 --> 00:51:35,632
Why am I so scared?

1199
00:51:36,132 --> 00:51:37,434
It's understandable.

1200
00:51:38,468 --> 00:51:39,936
It's driving me crazy.

1201
00:51:43,375 --> 00:51:48,848
(She's too scared to climb.)

1202
00:51:53,768 --> 00:51:55,418
Everyone is just wearing slippers.

1203
00:51:56,628 --> 00:51:59,628
(Locals are just wearing slippers.)

1204
00:52:00,682 --> 00:52:03,026
No way. Am I the only one scared?

1205
00:52:05,495 --> 00:52:07,197
We can do this!

1206
00:52:12,826 --> 00:52:14,304
- Yes!
- Let's go.

1207
00:52:14,600 --> 00:52:16,046
(They work up the courage
and slowly start climbing.)

1208
00:52:16,047 --> 00:52:16,906
Let's go.

1209
00:52:17,607 --> 00:52:19,876
- We'll go slowly.
- Okay.

1210
00:52:21,244 --> 00:52:24,814
One step at a time.

1211
00:52:25,744 --> 00:52:28,304
(Cautiously)

1212
00:52:29,452 --> 00:52:31,087
Step by step.

1213
00:52:31,488 --> 00:52:32,522
One step at a time.

1214
00:52:32,892 --> 00:52:34,257
It's okay.

1215
00:52:34,624 --> 00:52:36,126
You're good!

1216
00:52:37,494 --> 00:52:39,494
You're fine.

1217
00:52:39,794 --> 00:52:42,098
It's okay. You can do this.

1218
00:52:42,174 --> 00:52:44,414
- We can do this.
- We can do it.

1219
00:52:44,415 --> 00:52:46,770
If it gets too hard, let us know.

1220
00:52:47,675 --> 00:52:49,506
- Could you hold this for me?
- Sure!

1221
00:52:50,206 --> 00:52:51,875
Let's take our time.

1222
00:52:53,543 --> 00:52:55,712
- Can you hold it?
- Yes.

1223
00:52:55,713 --> 00:52:57,906
(The younger members hold
Gabee's cameras.)

1224
00:52:58,314 --> 00:53:00,491
- It's okay. We can do it.
- We can do it!

1225
00:53:00,492 --> 00:53:02,986
Gabee, you can do this.

1226
00:53:02,987 --> 00:53:04,354
You got this.

1227
00:53:04,393 --> 00:53:05,355
You're okay.

1228
00:53:06,307 --> 00:53:08,224
Just focus on what's in front of you.

1229
00:53:08,427 --> 00:53:09,592
I can do it.

1230
00:53:10,660 --> 00:53:13,229
To be honest, I'm scared
that no one is behind me.

1231
00:53:14,540 --> 00:53:15,598
I can do it.

1232
00:53:16,600 --> 00:53:19,067
- I can do it!
- You can do this, Queen Gabee!

1233
00:53:19,068 --> 00:53:20,370
You can do it.

1234
00:53:20,547 --> 00:53:22,706
- Let's do it.
- I can do this!

1235
00:53:22,707 --> 00:53:23,907
You can do it!

1236
00:53:25,241 --> 00:53:27,811
Let's go make a wish!

1237
00:53:28,080 --> 00:53:30,180
- It will grant our wishes.
- I know.

1238
00:53:30,240 --> 00:53:32,115
- It will.
- It'll definitely grant our wishes.

1239
00:53:33,160 --> 00:53:34,784
We're almost there.

1240
00:53:35,093 --> 00:53:37,087
We're halfway there.

1241
00:53:37,440 --> 00:53:38,788
We're more than halfway up.

1242
00:53:38,789 --> 00:53:40,203
(Less than half the stairs left)

1243
00:53:41,136 --> 00:53:42,158
I can do it.

1244
00:53:44,661 --> 00:53:46,730
- Wait.
- It's okay.

1245
00:53:48,021 --> 00:53:49,032
I can do it.

1246
00:53:49,033 --> 00:53:51,033
- Let's take a break. Take your time.
- I got this.

1247
00:53:51,541 --> 00:53:52,969
- You can do this.
- You can.

1248
00:53:53,307 --> 00:53:54,447
(Sniffling)

1249
00:54:00,440 --> 00:54:01,304
It's okay.

1250
00:54:01,305 --> 00:54:02,941
(Gabee gets upset and starts tearing up.)

1251
00:54:03,694 --> 00:54:04,781
Let's do this.

1252
00:54:05,548 --> 00:54:07,484
- Shall we go down together?
- No.

1253
00:54:09,261 --> 00:54:10,828
(Sad)

1254
00:54:12,288 --> 00:54:14,288
- Let's go.
- It's okay.

1255
00:54:14,289 --> 00:54:16,608
(She pushes through and keeps climbing.)

1256
00:54:17,703 --> 00:54:19,896
We're all doing well.

1257
00:54:28,351 --> 00:54:37,028
(Just a little further,
and they'll get an amazing view.)

1258
00:54:43,182 --> 00:54:45,182
This is nothing, right?

1259
00:54:45,183 --> 00:54:47,183
- It's nothing!
- This is huge!

1260
00:54:47,196 --> 00:54:48,758
- It's huge.
- Yes.

1261
00:54:49,009 --> 00:54:49,959
Seriously.

1262
00:54:50,176 --> 00:54:53,263
You're going beyond your limits.

1263
00:54:53,730 --> 00:54:58,101
You're climbing really high up
in the mountains.

1264
00:54:58,128 --> 00:55:00,270
I'm so tired. This is something.

1265
00:55:00,661 --> 00:55:01,805
I'm scared.

1266
00:55:02,238 --> 00:55:04,607
We got your back!

1267
00:55:05,642 --> 00:55:08,745
Two of us are right behind you.

1268
00:55:09,979 --> 00:55:12,282
She's right! We're so close.

1269
00:55:12,916 --> 00:55:14,217
We're not that far now.

1270
00:55:14,218 --> 00:55:15,613
We did it.

1271
00:55:16,186 --> 00:55:18,788
- We're almost there.
- We're almost done.

1272
00:55:18,789 --> 00:55:20,826
(They're almost at the top!)

1273
00:55:22,859 --> 00:55:24,093
My goodness!

1274
00:55:26,645 --> 00:55:28,665
Okay, Gabee. We're done.

1275
00:55:29,866 --> 00:55:31,034
Take it slow.

1276
00:55:31,835 --> 00:55:36,673
- In 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.
- In 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

1277
00:55:37,066 --> 00:55:38,959
(They made it to the top!)

1278
00:55:39,006 --> 00:55:40,143
Let's get this over with.

1279
00:55:40,410 --> 00:55:42,645
We did it!

1280
00:55:43,780 --> 00:55:44,981
We did it.

1281
00:55:44,982 --> 00:55:48,935
- Be careful.
- We made it. Let's go somewhere flat.

1282
00:55:49,355 --> 00:55:52,255
Oh, my. Let's sit down here.

1283
00:55:53,329 --> 00:55:58,848
(They see a breathtaking view at the top.)

1284
00:55:59,701 --> 00:56:00,964
I'm so proud of you.

1285
00:56:02,248 --> 00:56:04,067
I'm so sorry.

1286
00:56:04,368 --> 00:56:05,501
This is nothing.

1287
00:56:05,555 --> 00:56:07,437
We made it together, Gabee.

1288
00:56:08,571 --> 00:56:10,607
- It makes me cry too.
- I know.

1289
00:56:16,412 --> 00:56:18,548
Why am I crying too?

1290
00:56:20,066 --> 00:56:21,317
Was I the only one scared?

1291
00:56:21,332 --> 00:56:23,119
It was just me, right?

1292
00:56:23,486 --> 00:56:24,988
I wasn't scared.

1293
00:56:25,173 --> 00:56:27,173
- I'm being honest.
- I'm the only one scared.

1294
00:56:27,174 --> 00:56:28,979
- It wasn't scary.
- It's not scary.

1295
00:56:28,980 --> 00:56:30,593
I was terrified.

1296
00:56:31,394 --> 00:56:33,830
You pushed past your limits...

1297
00:56:33,831 --> 00:56:34,964
- True.
- on this trip.

1298
00:56:35,084 --> 00:56:36,299
We all did.

1299
00:56:37,478 --> 00:56:40,336
I was too scared to even walk up here.

1300
00:56:40,778 --> 00:56:43,273
Let's stay here. This is the main part.

1301
00:56:43,940 --> 00:56:45,275
This is the main area.

1302
00:56:45,417 --> 00:56:48,044
It's over. We're here.

1303
00:56:49,084 --> 00:56:51,080
Anyway, we did it!

1304
00:56:51,963 --> 00:56:54,757
(They successfully climbed Mount Bromo.)

1305
00:56:54,883 --> 00:56:56,219
We've come a long way.

1306
00:56:57,720 --> 00:56:59,889
- We really have.
- We did it.

1307
00:57:01,875 --> 00:57:03,493
By the way, look down there.

1308
00:57:06,826 --> 00:57:08,599
(Peeking)

1309
00:57:09,098 --> 00:57:11,634
It sounds like a waterfall.

1310
00:57:12,302 --> 00:57:15,104
The sound of magma bubbling.

1311
00:57:15,746 --> 00:57:17,273
It's super deep.

1312
00:57:19,044 --> 00:57:20,643
It really sounds like a waterfall.

1313
00:57:21,857 --> 00:57:23,880
It smells like a fart.

1314
00:57:24,380 --> 00:57:25,949
It smells like poop.

1315
00:57:26,916 --> 00:57:28,916
So it's not horse poop.

1316
00:57:29,435 --> 00:57:32,155
It's the sulfur smell coming
from down there.

1317
00:57:32,948 --> 00:57:34,324
That's so fascinating.

1318
00:57:35,191 --> 00:57:38,795
- This is different from what I thought.
- I agree.

1319
00:57:39,729 --> 00:57:41,464
You thought it'd be boiling, right?

1320
00:57:43,533 --> 00:57:44,467
Oh, my.

1321
00:57:47,737 --> 00:57:51,274
Now that we're up here, let's make a wish.

1322
00:57:51,275 --> 00:57:52,475
- Okay.
- Yes.

1323
00:57:52,897 --> 00:57:54,369
(They have to walk a little further
to the wishing spot.)

1324
00:57:54,370 --> 00:57:55,478
Shall we go see?

1325
00:57:55,729 --> 00:57:58,506
Let's try, and if it's too scary,
let's turn around.

1326
00:58:00,183 --> 00:58:01,584
- Shall we try?
- You girls go.

1327
00:58:01,657 --> 00:58:04,187
- Let's go slowly.
- I'll see if I want to go.

1328
00:58:04,524 --> 00:58:06,122
(Gasping)

1329
00:58:06,297 --> 00:58:07,390
It's a bit scary.

1330
00:58:07,444 --> 00:58:09,826
She'll be fine
if she keeps looking straight ahead.

1331
00:58:11,461 --> 00:58:13,363
- She shouldn't look left.
- Right?

1332
00:58:14,364 --> 00:58:16,065
She might still be scared.

1333
00:58:20,370 --> 00:58:21,404
Oh, dear.

1334
00:58:21,405 --> 00:58:25,764
(A narrow trail
with nothing on either side)

1335
00:58:26,042 --> 00:58:27,210
I'm scared.

1336
00:58:29,612 --> 00:58:31,781
- This...
- It might be scary.

1337
00:58:35,097 --> 00:58:37,097
(Arriving in front of the statue)

1338
00:58:37,098 --> 00:58:38,354
Here it is.

1339
00:58:40,545 --> 00:58:41,624
An elephant?

1340
00:58:41,625 --> 00:58:44,584
(A Ganesha statue that grants wishes)

1341
00:58:45,495 --> 00:58:47,797
I really feel like it'll make
my wish come true.

1342
00:58:47,966 --> 00:58:49,966
Should we tell her to...

1343
00:58:51,933 --> 00:58:53,703
Let's discuss it with her.

1344
00:58:53,704 --> 00:58:55,286
Let's tell her not to look to her left.

1345
00:58:55,287 --> 00:58:56,627
(Heading back)

1346
00:58:57,440 --> 00:59:00,309
She was even struggling on the stairs.

1347
00:59:01,878 --> 00:59:04,213
This might be too scary for her.

1348
00:59:05,615 --> 00:59:07,615
It's not really slippery on the way.

1349
00:59:07,616 --> 00:59:09,616
- It's not slippery.
- But it's narrow, right?

1350
00:59:09,695 --> 00:59:13,121
You can see on the sides too.

1351
00:59:13,122 --> 00:59:14,515
She's probably better off staying here.

1352
00:59:14,516 --> 00:59:16,791
Let's stay here. It's nicer here.

1353
00:59:16,792 --> 00:59:19,128
- The view behind us is nice too.
- Right.

1354
00:59:19,395 --> 00:59:22,131
Since we're up here anyway,
let's make a wish.

1355
00:59:22,132 --> 00:59:24,132
I feel like our wishes will
really come true.

1356
00:59:24,133 --> 00:59:25,001
I think so too.

1357
00:59:25,002 --> 00:59:28,171
Because we all put our hearts
into our wishes.

1358
00:59:28,172 --> 00:59:29,072
Right.

1359
00:59:31,481 --> 00:59:33,810
Since we all came together
with our whole hearts.

1360
00:59:33,811 --> 00:59:36,279
(Dori hands out the flowers
they bought at the entrance.)

1361
00:59:36,280 --> 00:59:37,613
- Okay.
- What was this?

1362
00:59:37,914 --> 00:59:39,421
This was Gabee's.

1363
00:59:39,422 --> 00:59:40,383
No, it's mine.

1364
00:59:40,534 --> 00:59:41,551
This is Gabee's.

1365
00:59:41,552 --> 00:59:43,386
- This is yours.
- Okay!

1366
00:59:44,354 --> 00:59:45,955
Let's make a wish.

1367
00:59:48,987 --> 00:59:53,970
(They each make a wish in their hearts.)

1368
00:59:59,377 --> 01:00:00,629
(Opening her eyes)

1369
01:00:00,654 --> 01:00:02,221
(Excited)

1370
01:00:02,833 --> 01:00:07,069
(Can't resist goofing around)

1371
01:00:08,605 --> 01:00:10,339
(Patting)

1372
01:00:10,340 --> 01:00:12,508
It'll all come true.

1373
01:00:13,342 --> 01:00:15,244
Okay, did everyone make a wish?

1374
01:00:15,245 --> 01:00:16,245
- Yes!
- Yes!

1375
01:00:16,513 --> 01:00:19,181
May they all come true!

1376
01:00:19,182 --> 01:00:20,483
Our wish is...

1377
01:00:20,484 --> 01:00:22,017
This!

1378
01:00:22,018 --> 01:00:23,319
- And this!
- This!

1379
01:00:23,887 --> 01:00:25,421
On three?

1380
01:00:25,422 --> 01:00:26,355
- Yes!
- Yes!

1381
01:00:26,356 --> 01:00:27,790
One, two, three!

1382
01:00:27,791 --> 01:00:28,791
Let's go!

1383
01:00:28,792 --> 01:00:31,327
Let's go! Make it all come true!

1384
01:00:33,096 --> 01:00:34,430
(Throwing the wishing flowers
as hard as they can)

1385
01:00:34,431 --> 01:00:37,100
Goal!

1386
01:00:39,770 --> 01:00:42,271
- Please!
- It's going to come true!

1387
01:00:42,272 --> 01:00:44,006
It'll all come true!

1388
01:00:44,408 --> 01:00:46,608
We did it!

1389
01:00:46,609 --> 01:00:49,445
Wow, I'm tearing up!

1390
01:00:52,716 --> 01:00:54,951
(Now even the youngest is in tears.)

1391
01:00:54,952 --> 01:00:56,319
She's crying too!

1392
01:00:56,787 --> 01:00:58,121
Wow.

1393
01:00:58,122 --> 01:00:59,088
I get it!

1394
01:01:00,590 --> 01:01:01,857
I get it now.

1395
01:01:02,192 --> 01:01:03,159
(Crying)

1396
01:01:03,860 --> 01:01:05,327
Harimu worked the hardest.

1397
01:01:05,328 --> 01:01:07,831
The youngest always gets stuck
with the heavy lifting!

1398
01:01:07,856 --> 01:01:09,299
Our youngest, you worked hard!

1399
01:01:09,324 --> 01:01:10,966
(Bittersweet feelings at their final stop)

1400
01:01:12,969 --> 01:01:15,437
I'm so overwhelmed.

1401
01:01:17,041 --> 01:01:19,007
Anything is possible.
You just have to go for it.

1402
01:01:19,008 --> 01:01:21,577
- That's so true.
- What a moment.

1403
01:01:21,845 --> 01:01:23,846
Let's make one wish together.

1404
01:01:23,847 --> 01:01:24,713
(Making one last wish together)

1405
01:01:25,082 --> 01:01:26,416
Let's stay healthy.

1406
01:01:26,417 --> 01:01:27,417
- Yes.
- Yes.

1407
01:01:27,418 --> 01:01:29,052
- And happy.
- Happy.

1408
01:01:29,053 --> 01:01:32,321
And we hope everyone watching
stays healthy and happy too.

1409
01:01:32,322 --> 01:01:34,524
- Yeah.
- Yes, our dear viewers.

1410
01:01:34,825 --> 01:01:38,361
- I'm getting all choked up.
- Tell me about it.

1411
01:01:38,362 --> 01:01:40,329
- We all did so great.
- Great job, everyone.

1412
01:01:40,330 --> 01:01:41,531
Yeah.

1413
01:01:41,532 --> 01:01:43,699
How about we yell
"I love you" on three and toss it?

1414
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:45,868
- Sounds good.
- One, two, three!

1415
01:01:45,869 --> 01:01:47,470
- I love you!
- I love you!

1416
01:01:50,041 --> 01:01:50,941
Okay, let's go!

1417
01:01:51,041 --> 01:01:52,508
It's flying!

1418
01:01:52,509 --> 01:01:54,711
- Over there!
- It's going down!

1419
01:01:54,712 --> 01:01:57,113
Alright, let's head out!

1420
01:01:58,108 --> 01:01:59,274
Wow, look at that.

1421
01:01:59,382 --> 01:02:00,549
Look at that.

1422
01:02:00,550 --> 01:02:01,750
What is that?

1423
01:02:01,751 --> 01:02:04,028
I think our wishes are actually
being granted!

1424
01:02:04,053 --> 01:02:05,854
- A little whirlwind just kicked up.
- Really?

1425
01:02:05,867 --> 01:02:06,489
Yeah.

1426
01:02:06,661 --> 01:02:08,657
A whirlwind! Did you catch that?

1427
01:02:09,159 --> 01:02:11,227
The genie is coming!

1428
01:02:12,362 --> 01:02:16,065
- Great job.
- We got so much tougher.

1429
01:02:16,233 --> 01:02:19,435
I'd like to stop getting
tougher now, though!

1430
01:02:21,471 --> 01:02:24,206
- Okay.
- We're all done with wishes.

1431
01:02:25,175 --> 01:02:28,444
Let's take it slow as we head down.

1432
01:02:28,612 --> 01:02:30,980
- Gabee, don't worry. I'm here.
- Yes.

1433
01:02:31,614 --> 01:02:33,583
(Taking it slow
with everyone cheering them on)

1434
01:02:33,584 --> 01:02:34,817
I can do this. Piece of cake.

1435
01:02:35,285 --> 01:02:36,952
It's nothing. You've got this.

1436
01:02:36,953 --> 01:02:38,194
Just keep your eyes glued to the ground.

1437
01:02:38,219 --> 01:02:39,355
Eyes on the ground, Gabee.

1438
01:02:39,356 --> 01:02:41,557
Nicely done. You're halfway there!

1439
01:02:41,558 --> 01:02:43,018
You're doing awesome.

1440
01:02:43,043 --> 01:02:45,160
Hold up, emergency! Just a second.

1441
01:02:45,729 --> 01:02:47,296
One second.

1442
01:02:47,464 --> 01:02:49,098
- Keep your eyes on the ground!
- Okay!

1443
01:02:49,099 --> 01:02:50,699
You're almost there!

1444
01:02:51,100 --> 01:02:52,768
- Eyes down!
- Yes, you did it.

1445
01:02:55,239 --> 01:02:56,705
Keep your eyes on the ground!

1446
01:02:57,875 --> 01:03:00,376
Keep your eyes on the ground, Gabee!

1447
01:03:00,377 --> 01:03:02,978
Watch your step, okay?

1448
01:03:03,346 --> 01:03:06,014
- Eyes on the ground!
- Let's go.

1449
01:03:07,217 --> 01:03:09,218
A purple-pink sky. That's unreal.

1450
01:03:14,524 --> 01:03:16,391
We should be able to spot the stars now.

1451
01:03:16,926 --> 01:03:17,827
Look over there.

1452
01:03:18,194 --> 01:03:19,294
Already?

1453
01:03:20,698 --> 01:03:22,931
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1454
01:03:25,435 --> 01:03:29,538
(Leaving the volcano
behind and heading back)

1455
01:03:29,539 --> 01:03:30,739
- Dori!
- Yes?

1456
01:03:30,740 --> 01:03:34,276
How long until we get to...

1457
01:03:34,277 --> 01:03:35,411
- The hotel?
- Yeah, the hotel.

1458
01:03:35,412 --> 01:03:36,345
Five minutes.

1459
01:03:37,447 --> 01:03:38,779
- Dori.
- Yes?

1460
01:03:38,780 --> 01:03:40,883
How was the trip for you?

1461
01:03:41,918 --> 01:03:43,886
- How was it?
- I'm so happy because...

1462
01:03:43,887 --> 01:03:45,319
- I think...
- Yeah.

1463
01:03:45,344 --> 01:03:46,756
everything went so smoothly!

1464
01:03:47,090 --> 01:03:50,192
- Yeah!
- You did an amazing job today!

1465
01:03:50,193 --> 01:03:51,860
- You think so?
- Absolutely!

1466
01:03:51,861 --> 01:03:53,195
Best guide ever!

1467
01:03:53,196 --> 01:03:55,698
Like I told you earlier,
I was super nervous today.

1468
01:03:55,699 --> 01:03:57,199
Yeah, we know.

1469
01:03:57,200 --> 01:03:59,468
Thank you so much.

1470
01:03:59,469 --> 01:04:00,903
Thank you. You pulled it off!

1471
01:04:01,404 --> 01:04:02,571
You did fantastic!

1472
01:04:02,572 --> 01:04:04,173
As long as you weren't disappointed,

1473
01:04:04,174 --> 01:04:05,507
it's a huge win for me.

1474
01:04:05,508 --> 01:04:09,611
(Chatting with Dori about the trip
as they drive)

1475
01:04:09,612 --> 01:04:10,680
Yes.

1476
01:04:11,015 --> 01:04:14,015
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

1477
01:04:14,016 --> 01:04:14,983
(Arriving at the hotel)

1478
01:04:14,984 --> 01:04:17,320
Gabee, thank you very much.

1479
01:04:17,687 --> 01:04:19,554
Won Ji, thank you very much.

1480
01:04:19,555 --> 01:04:21,189
Harimu, thank you very much.

1481
01:04:21,190 --> 01:04:22,324
Sian, thank you.

1482
01:04:23,193 --> 01:04:26,396
- Dori! Thank you so much!
- Thank you, Dori!

1483
01:04:27,230 --> 01:04:28,430
See you again!

1484
01:04:28,598 --> 01:04:30,599
- Bye-bye!
- See you again!

1485
01:04:30,934 --> 01:04:32,701
He remembered every single name.

1486
01:04:33,169 --> 01:04:35,237
- I'm so touched.
- That's so sweet of him.

1487
01:04:36,473 --> 01:04:38,240
It's really over.

1488
01:04:38,241 --> 01:04:40,043
- We made it.
- Good job, everyone.

1489
01:04:40,044 --> 01:04:43,813
- It's officially wrapped.
- Everything is done, indeed.

1490
01:04:43,814 --> 01:04:45,849
Great job, everyone.

1491
01:04:45,850 --> 01:04:47,774
Great job.

1492
01:04:47,918 --> 01:04:51,320
- Seriously, such good work.
- Yeah.

1493
01:04:51,321 --> 01:04:53,589
- You guys are all incredible.
- Your eyes are so puffy!

1494
01:04:55,392 --> 01:04:56,692
- Unreal.
- Right?

1495
01:04:56,693 --> 01:04:57,693
Every single one of you.

1496
01:04:57,694 --> 01:04:59,395
(Congratulating each other
on making it through)

1497
01:04:59,396 --> 01:05:00,363
We're amazing.

1498
01:05:00,397 --> 01:05:02,698
Let's go get cleaned up.

1499
01:05:03,233 --> 01:05:04,500
You go first.

1500
01:05:04,501 --> 01:05:06,368
I'll be out in five minutes.

1501
01:05:06,803 --> 01:05:09,838
I think I just need to brush the dust off.

1502
01:05:10,774 --> 01:05:11,607
Who wants moisturizer?

1503
01:05:11,608 --> 01:05:13,042
- Me!
- Me!

1504
01:05:14,044 --> 01:05:16,379
- Save some for me after I wash up!
- Here you go.

1505
01:05:16,380 --> 01:05:19,081
We've been using this cream...

1506
01:05:19,883 --> 01:05:20,950
for over a week now.

1507
01:05:20,951 --> 01:05:22,384
Literally the only thing we've used.

1508
01:05:22,385 --> 01:05:24,887
- That's wild.
- My skin actually looks better.

1509
01:05:24,888 --> 01:05:27,223
- Right?
- My skin always freaks out when I travel.

1510
01:05:27,224 --> 01:05:29,425
It's so good for soothing irritated skin.

1511
01:05:29,759 --> 01:05:31,426
Look at us, we're all glowing!

1512
01:05:31,427 --> 01:05:32,594
I told you this stuff is pure gold.

1513
01:05:32,595 --> 01:05:33,762
Are we all skin models now?

1514
01:05:33,763 --> 01:05:35,064
Our skin is seriously radiant.

1515
01:05:35,465 --> 01:05:36,765
We're a whole skin-care girl group.

1516
01:05:36,766 --> 01:05:38,100
(Skin beauty group)

1517
01:05:38,101 --> 01:05:40,069
This cream saved our skin.

1518
01:05:40,437 --> 01:05:41,270
Thank you.

1519
01:05:41,738 --> 01:05:42,914
My skin feels so firm and plump.

1520
01:05:42,939 --> 01:05:45,874
All you need is this one jar!

1521
01:05:46,776 --> 01:05:48,878
We've got to pack all this up, right?

1522
01:05:49,212 --> 01:05:52,514
We'll probably need to fold
the laundry flat to save space.

1523
01:05:53,717 --> 01:05:55,885
- Shall we start packing?
- Yeah.

1524
01:05:56,152 --> 01:05:58,288
We've all got our designated
spots for everything.

1525
01:05:58,888 --> 01:06:01,756
Final packing before we fly back to Korea.

1526
01:06:02,939 --> 01:06:04,159
(The long-awaited final packing)

1527
01:06:04,160 --> 01:06:05,694
The grand finale of packing.

1528
01:06:05,695 --> 01:06:08,397
It feels like forever
since we last saw our suitcases.

1529
01:06:08,531 --> 01:06:11,766
I feel like we're pro packers now.

1530
01:06:11,767 --> 01:06:14,836
Everyone has an exact spot for their gear.

1531
01:06:14,837 --> 01:06:15,905
- Totally.
- Yeah.

1532
01:06:16,306 --> 01:06:17,773
- Down to a science.
- Yeah.

1533
01:06:17,774 --> 01:06:19,541
- My bag.
- Right.

1534
01:06:19,542 --> 01:06:21,110
We really cleared out a ton of stuff.

1535
01:06:21,277 --> 01:06:22,510
- We honestly did.
- Yes.

1536
01:06:23,380 --> 01:06:25,036
We ditched so much,

1537
01:06:25,060 --> 01:06:27,116
you'd never guess
how much we started with.

1538
01:06:27,884 --> 01:06:29,051
It's all cleared out.

1539
01:06:29,052 --> 01:06:30,653
- It's practically empty.
- Totally cleaned out.

1540
01:06:30,654 --> 01:06:32,054
Where did my pouch go?

1541
01:06:32,055 --> 01:06:33,522
That is so true.

1542
01:06:33,857 --> 01:06:36,826
At first, we were like,

1543
01:06:36,827 --> 01:06:39,128
"We don't have this!
What are we supposed to do?"

1544
01:06:39,129 --> 01:06:41,664
Then we just kept letting things go.

1545
01:06:41,665 --> 01:06:42,998
And it wasn't even uncomfortable.

1546
01:06:42,999 --> 01:06:45,401
We didn't even touch shampoo just now.

1547
01:06:45,402 --> 01:06:46,602
Just washed everything off
with facial cleanser.

1548
01:06:46,603 --> 01:06:47,870
One face wash for the whole deal.

1549
01:06:47,871 --> 01:06:50,472
I've never used a facial cleanser
as body wash before.

1550
01:06:50,473 --> 01:06:53,275
There was just the one bottle
in the bathroom.

1551
01:06:53,610 --> 01:06:55,744
Turns out, it totally works.

1552
01:06:55,745 --> 01:06:58,013
You make do with what you've got.

1553
01:06:58,014 --> 01:06:59,515
We're unstoppable now.

1554
01:06:59,516 --> 01:07:01,150
Nothing even feels like a hassle anymore.

1555
01:07:01,151 --> 01:07:02,519
We leveled up!

1556
01:07:03,119 --> 01:07:05,554
(Leveled up to tougher women!)

1557
01:07:05,555 --> 01:07:07,556
Was there any item...

1558
01:07:08,124 --> 01:07:10,292
you were extra glad you packed?

1559
01:07:10,293 --> 01:07:12,260
Something you ended up using non-stop?

1560
01:07:12,529 --> 01:07:14,697
For me,

1561
01:07:14,773 --> 01:07:17,633
- definitely the UV cooling sleeves.
- Oh, totally.

1562
01:07:18,268 --> 01:07:19,735
So glad I brought those.

1563
01:07:19,736 --> 01:07:22,438
I used them pretty much everywhere.

1564
01:07:22,439 --> 01:07:24,139
- Total lifesavers.
- What else?

1565
01:07:24,407 --> 01:07:26,375
Honestly,

1566
01:07:26,843 --> 01:07:28,110
this quarter-zip.

1567
01:07:28,878 --> 01:07:30,880
- Oh, absolutely.
- We shot 10 episodes, right?

1568
01:07:31,448 --> 01:07:33,982
I'm pretty sure
I wore it for like 8 of them.

1569
01:07:33,983 --> 01:07:35,484
Yeah, that one!

1570
01:07:35,485 --> 01:07:37,252
This one too. And I'm still wearing it!

1571
01:07:37,253 --> 01:07:38,249
Right?

1572
01:07:38,250 --> 01:07:39,489
For me, it's got to be this.

1573
01:07:39,789 --> 01:07:41,356
For me, that brown top.

1574
01:07:41,357 --> 01:07:42,236
Did you realize...

1575
01:07:42,261 --> 01:07:43,725
we all left Korea
wearing these exact outfits?

1576
01:07:43,726 --> 01:07:44,960
I was wearing this on day one!

1577
01:07:44,961 --> 01:07:46,061
You're so right!

1578
01:07:46,696 --> 01:07:49,998
We basically lived
in our airport clothes the whole trip.

1579
01:07:49,999 --> 01:07:52,034
And now we're wearing them
right back home.

1580
01:07:52,035 --> 01:07:53,702
- Yup.
- Heading home in the same fit.

1581
01:07:53,703 --> 01:07:55,137
(Coming full circle)

1582
01:07:55,138 --> 01:07:58,440
Next time we travel,
we're definitely packing way lighter.

1583
01:07:58,441 --> 01:07:59,941
- For sure.
- Just one spare outfit?

1584
01:08:00,176 --> 01:08:01,343
Just one?

1585
01:08:01,544 --> 01:08:04,078
How about a sensible three-pack?

1586
01:08:04,079 --> 01:08:05,580
Because honestly,

1587
01:08:05,581 --> 01:08:07,549
you never ended up wearing your dress.

1588
01:08:07,550 --> 01:08:09,852
And I never touched my ladybug tee.

1589
01:08:09,853 --> 01:08:10,919
- That dress!
- You're right.

1590
01:08:10,920 --> 01:08:12,954
- It's still untouched, isn't it?
- Yep.

1591
01:08:12,955 --> 01:08:14,256
Yeah.

1592
01:08:14,257 --> 01:08:16,625
(The princess dress she never got to wear)

1593
01:08:17,528 --> 01:08:19,228
I truly didn't need this.

1594
01:08:21,364 --> 01:08:23,433
Oh!

1595
01:08:23,434 --> 01:08:24,355
This right here!

1596
01:08:24,379 --> 01:08:26,902
Hands down one of the best things
we packed.

1597
01:08:26,903 --> 01:08:28,403
Yes, 100 percent.

1598
01:08:28,404 --> 01:08:30,772
We used this just to hit the bathroom
in the jungle.

1599
01:08:30,773 --> 01:08:34,009
- Exactly.
- And whenever we shot our videos.

1600
01:08:34,577 --> 01:08:36,244
Let's make sure that's packed
nice and safe.

1601
01:08:36,245 --> 01:08:37,312
(Unexpected MVP that made it to the end)

1602
01:08:37,313 --> 01:08:38,980
The unsung MVP.

1603
01:08:39,582 --> 01:08:42,083
- We have to pack this too.
- Oh, right!

1604
01:08:42,084 --> 01:08:43,318
Yes, this.

1605
01:08:43,319 --> 01:08:44,753
A little keepsake.

1606
01:08:44,754 --> 01:08:47,188
And our rings!

1607
01:08:47,189 --> 01:08:49,090
Friendship rings too!

1608
01:08:49,692 --> 01:08:52,827
(A friendship item made even
more special by sharing it)

1609
01:08:53,463 --> 01:08:54,830
This one too!

1610
01:08:56,032 --> 01:08:57,666
Oh, yeah!

1611
01:08:58,667 --> 01:08:59,634
Ta-da!

1612
01:08:59,969 --> 01:09:02,037
I'm definitely hanging this up in my room.

1613
01:09:02,038 --> 01:09:04,739
- That feels like ages ago.
- Secret Santa too.

1614
01:09:04,740 --> 01:09:07,609
We planned it on day one...

1615
01:09:07,610 --> 01:09:09,377
and did the reveal on day two!

1616
01:09:09,378 --> 01:09:11,580
- These hats too.
- Yes, hats.

1617
01:09:11,581 --> 01:09:13,982
- They were permanently tucked away.
- That's so true.

1618
01:09:15,818 --> 01:09:17,033
It's so pretty, though.

1619
01:09:17,058 --> 01:09:18,696
(Hats that never left the suitcase)

1620
01:09:18,721 --> 01:09:20,922
Something I kept on me
in my personal bag the whole time.

1621
01:09:20,923 --> 01:09:21,990
Oh, that!

1622
01:09:21,991 --> 01:09:23,825
- This one's from Fin.
- Yeah.

1623
01:09:23,826 --> 01:09:26,628
- And this is from Ipu.
- From Ipu.

1624
01:09:26,629 --> 01:09:27,696
(Gifts Fin and Ipu gave them)

1625
01:09:27,697 --> 01:09:29,632
I'm tucking them right in here.

1626
01:09:29,633 --> 01:09:30,765
My little keepsakes.

1627
01:09:30,766 --> 01:09:33,401
They're all so tiny.

1628
01:09:34,604 --> 01:09:37,406
This is straight from the jungle.

1629
01:09:37,674 --> 01:09:39,341
He handed this over
and told us to take a sniff.

1630
01:09:39,342 --> 01:09:40,141
(Wow)

1631
01:09:40,142 --> 01:09:42,143
- Really?
- It's still here.

1632
01:09:42,144 --> 01:09:43,211
Oh, wow.

1633
01:09:43,212 --> 01:09:46,214
- That's amazing!
- Ipu handed it to us.

1634
01:09:46,215 --> 01:09:50,552
(A betel nut leaf
straight from the jungle)

1635
01:09:51,487 --> 01:09:54,155
- Guess I really liked it.
- Yeah, you must've loved it.

1636
01:09:54,156 --> 01:09:55,256
(The scent is gone,
but the memories stay.)

1637
01:09:55,391 --> 01:09:58,026
Ipu, Fin, and Dori.

1638
01:09:58,051 --> 01:09:59,618
I'm really going to miss them.

1639
01:09:59,962 --> 01:10:03,913
They treated us
with so much genuine warmth.

1640
01:10:03,914 --> 01:10:05,768
- They really did.
- You could truly feel it.

1641
01:10:06,035 --> 01:10:11,107
I'm really going to miss them.

1642
01:10:11,333 --> 01:10:13,242
We made quite a few friends
along the way too.

1643
01:10:13,391 --> 01:10:14,610
Three whole friends.

1644
01:10:15,971 --> 01:10:19,578
(Every single item is filled
with memories.)

1645
01:10:19,618 --> 01:10:21,484
Looking at all of this...

1646
01:10:21,531 --> 01:10:22,752
This is so us.

1647
01:10:23,636 --> 01:10:25,602
- It really feels like us.
- Totally.

1648
01:10:25,714 --> 01:10:26,923
All right, let's pack up.

1649
01:10:27,002 --> 01:10:29,158
- Ready to pack?
- Let's do it.

1650
01:10:30,526 --> 01:10:32,795
We really gathered a lot of stuff.

1651
01:10:33,436 --> 01:10:34,864
So many memories.

1652
01:10:36,933 --> 01:10:40,135
- This one made it...
- All the way to the end.

1653
01:10:41,182 --> 01:10:43,448
Next time, let's communicate through this.

1654
01:10:43,482 --> 01:10:44,307
Great idea!

1655
01:10:44,556 --> 01:10:47,310
I'm so glad we had this
from the very beginning.

1656
01:10:47,342 --> 01:10:48,129
Me too.

1657
01:10:48,130 --> 01:10:50,130
- She's so thoughtful.
- A travel journal.

1658
01:10:50,476 --> 01:10:51,614
Just in case.

1659
01:10:53,216 --> 01:10:55,216
It takes me right back
to when we first packed.

1660
01:10:55,551 --> 01:10:58,254
Should we each leave
one final note in here?

1661
01:10:58,378 --> 01:10:59,101
Love that.

1662
01:10:59,584 --> 01:11:01,944
(Taking turns writing
down their final thoughts)

1663
01:11:02,564 --> 01:11:05,817
(Deep in thought)

1664
01:11:05,997 --> 01:11:08,064
"This journey meant so much to me."

1665
01:11:08,564 --> 01:11:11,801
"Empty it out. Empty everything."

1666
01:11:14,070 --> 01:11:16,606
"What this journey taught me was..."

1667
01:11:16,607 --> 01:11:19,075
"the beauty of emptying out
and letting go."

1668
01:11:19,356 --> 01:11:22,078
"Yet, I'm heading home fuller than ever."

1669
01:11:22,845 --> 01:11:26,783
"Thank you for joining me
on this journey of letting go."

1670
01:11:26,927 --> 01:11:29,485
From here on, I'll fill my life
with what truly matters.

1671
01:11:29,486 --> 01:11:31,667
Terima kasih. Khop khun kha.

1672
01:11:33,756 --> 01:11:36,592
"It was such a meaningful trip,
and I learned so much."

1673
01:11:36,593 --> 01:11:40,396
"I don't think I've ever reflected
this deeply on myself while traveling."

1674
01:11:40,685 --> 01:11:43,399
"Won Ji, Sian, Harimu."

1675
01:11:43,596 --> 01:11:45,701
"I'm so grateful it was the four of us."

1676
01:11:45,789 --> 01:11:49,029
"Thank you for a trip
that helped me grow so much."

1677
01:11:52,369 --> 01:11:55,478
"At the very end, I made a wish."

1678
01:11:55,820 --> 01:12:00,149
"I want to live my whole life
the way we lived this journey."

1679
01:12:00,894 --> 01:12:04,587
"I was so happy
to be surrounded by people..."

1680
01:12:04,588 --> 01:12:07,623
"as dependable and lovely as you all."

1681
01:12:07,652 --> 01:12:09,959
"Love you."

1682
01:12:12,018 --> 01:12:14,429
(The youngest delivers
a heartfelt closing message.)

1683
01:12:14,498 --> 01:12:18,868
You wished to live life like this trip?

1684
01:12:19,135 --> 01:12:20,469
Yeah, at the very end.

1685
01:12:20,470 --> 01:12:22,271
- What a beautiful wish.
- That's so lovely.

1686
01:12:22,272 --> 01:12:23,409
(Beaming with pride)

1687
01:12:23,429 --> 01:12:24,440
To be honest,

1688
01:12:25,141 --> 01:12:30,046
I was so terrified I wouldn't be able
to finish the trip with you guys.

1689
01:12:30,067 --> 01:12:31,447
- Because you got sick?
- Yeah.

1690
01:12:31,848 --> 01:12:34,383
I was really worried,

1691
01:12:35,651 --> 01:12:38,221
and honestly,

1692
01:12:38,621 --> 01:12:41,757
I felt so terribly guilty
because I thought...

1693
01:12:41,839 --> 01:12:44,160
I ruined a whole day for everyone
because of me.

1694
01:12:45,721 --> 01:12:49,732
But when you wish for something
with all your heart, it really happens.

1695
01:12:50,099 --> 01:12:53,135
I wanted nothing more than to finish
this journey together with you all.

1696
01:12:53,160 --> 01:12:57,273
(The youngest opens up
about her true feelings.)

1697
01:12:57,386 --> 01:12:59,275
But then I bounced back immediately.

1698
01:12:59,436 --> 01:13:01,644
I just suddenly snapped back to life!

1699
01:13:01,645 --> 01:13:03,512
- Your resilience.
- My bounce-back ability.

1700
01:13:03,756 --> 01:13:05,181
Your recovery rate.

1701
01:13:05,182 --> 01:13:06,983
My recovery rate is legendary!

1702
01:13:06,984 --> 01:13:09,418
I think I was still a little delirious
when I said that.

1703
01:13:09,986 --> 01:13:11,986
Honestly, there were way more fun moments.

1704
01:13:11,987 --> 01:13:13,222
Oh, 100 percent.

1705
01:13:13,535 --> 01:13:17,627
Today wrapped up on such a dramatic note,

1706
01:13:18,661 --> 01:13:20,554
so I know it might seem that way,

1707
01:13:20,569 --> 01:13:24,000
but the jungle is
what really stuck with me.

1708
01:13:25,002 --> 01:13:26,869
It felt so refreshing.

1709
01:13:27,382 --> 01:13:30,206
I felt like I truly conquered
something in that jungle.

1710
01:13:30,362 --> 01:13:32,108
That's the truth of life, right there.

1711
01:13:32,508 --> 01:13:35,511
What seems like the worst
might not actually be the worst.

1712
01:13:35,776 --> 01:13:38,547
And what seems like the best
might not always be the best.

1713
01:13:38,548 --> 01:13:40,917
The jungle is what stayed in my heart.

1714
01:13:40,918 --> 01:13:43,491
(You never really know until you dive in.)

1715
01:13:43,617 --> 01:13:46,355
Every single second was
a challenge for me.

1716
01:13:46,689 --> 01:13:49,625
Looking back on my life so far,

1717
01:13:49,644 --> 01:13:51,960
whether traveling
or just in day-to-day life,

1718
01:13:52,762 --> 01:13:56,031
I always ran away from things
I didn't feel like doing.

1719
01:13:56,499 --> 01:13:58,499
But once I actually faced them,

1720
01:13:59,101 --> 01:14:02,783
so many of those things
turned out to be deeply rewarding.

1721
01:14:02,808 --> 01:14:05,608
Because of that, my confidence
and self-worth shot way up.

1722
01:14:06,061 --> 01:14:08,544
I learned so much.

1723
01:14:08,575 --> 01:14:11,521
I think I've built this mindset
of, "Just go for it first."

1724
01:14:11,522 --> 01:14:12,415
That's amazing.

1725
01:14:12,416 --> 01:14:14,951
I'm kind of the opposite.

1726
01:14:15,226 --> 01:14:18,721
For me, this kind of stuff is
just another Tuesday.

1727
01:14:18,746 --> 01:14:20,174
(Just everyday life
for travel creator Won Ji)

1728
01:14:20,199 --> 01:14:22,224
How have you spent
your whole life doing this?

1729
01:14:22,253 --> 01:14:25,206
I've been living like this for so long...

1730
01:14:25,207 --> 01:14:27,973
that I never stopped to think
it was anything special.

1731
01:14:27,974 --> 01:14:30,753
- Nothing extra special.
- I just brushed it off as routine.

1732
01:14:30,754 --> 01:14:34,303
But watching how genuinely thrilled
you guys were...

1733
01:14:35,174 --> 01:14:36,939
softened something inside me too.

1734
01:14:37,517 --> 01:14:39,920
- I totally get that.
- You gained a new appreciation.

1735
01:14:39,921 --> 01:14:44,447
It made me realize how much
I was taking all this for granted.

1736
01:14:45,560 --> 01:14:48,050
Just seeing you all so happy
made me genuinely happy.

1737
01:14:48,100 --> 01:14:49,218
Really?

1738
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:51,287
Wait, are you going to cry again?

1739
01:14:51,693 --> 01:14:52,838
(Oh no, what do I do?)

1740
01:14:52,865 --> 01:14:55,958
- Won Ji!
- You're going to make me lose it!

1741
01:14:56,820 --> 01:14:58,861
You're incredible.

1742
01:15:02,298 --> 01:15:04,133
You're such a wonderful person.

1743
01:15:04,151 --> 01:15:06,002
Quick, zoom in on this!

1744
01:15:07,318 --> 01:15:09,623
- She's such a variety show pro.
- Born for television!

1745
01:15:09,624 --> 01:15:11,007
Telling the camera to zoom in!

1746
01:15:11,507 --> 01:15:13,239
(Flustered)

1747
01:15:13,264 --> 01:15:17,103
We pushed through with so much strength...

1748
01:15:17,975 --> 01:15:19,779
because you kept us grounded
the whole time.

1749
01:15:19,804 --> 01:15:22,018
You're such an amazing big sister figure.

1750
01:15:22,198 --> 01:15:24,320
And you guys were
such wonderful younger sisters.

1751
01:15:24,418 --> 01:15:25,178
Thank you.

1752
01:15:25,179 --> 01:15:28,111
- We shared such an unforgettable journey.
- Absolutely.

1753
01:15:28,112 --> 01:15:29,225
We truly did.

1754
01:15:29,725 --> 01:15:32,194
I got so much positive energy
from both of you too.

1755
01:15:32,195 --> 01:15:33,129
Same here.

1756
01:15:33,164 --> 01:15:34,063
Seriously.

1757
01:15:34,511 --> 01:15:35,831
You influenced me so much.

1758
01:15:36,799 --> 01:15:38,334
I think we're just sad.

1759
01:15:38,591 --> 01:15:40,970
Sad that we're about
to go our separate ways.

1760
01:15:41,711 --> 01:15:43,039
- Don't say that!
- It's such a bummer.

1761
01:15:43,091 --> 01:15:44,471
We'll hang out in Korea.

1762
01:15:44,472 --> 01:15:48,944
- I'm actually so excited for that.
- But it won't feel the same in Seoul!

1763
01:15:49,140 --> 01:15:52,966
We won't be looking all disheveled
and covered in dirt like this!

1764
01:15:52,967 --> 01:15:55,017
- Disheveled?
- Grimy?

1765
01:15:55,160 --> 01:15:57,242
Either way, I loved every single second.

1766
01:15:57,243 --> 01:15:58,921
It was all about stripping down
to the essentials.

1767
01:15:58,922 --> 01:16:00,423
Total Abra-ca-Empty!

1768
01:16:01,070 --> 01:16:03,259
Yet we experienced so much,

1769
01:16:03,260 --> 01:16:05,988
and built such a special bond
with each other.

1770
01:16:05,989 --> 01:16:07,763
- Exactly.
- It's unbelievable.

1771
01:16:08,056 --> 01:16:10,666
We gained so much more
than whatever we left behind.

1772
01:16:10,691 --> 01:16:12,767
(Gaining so much more)

1773
01:16:18,125 --> 01:16:19,472
It's so bittersweet.

1774
01:16:19,619 --> 01:16:21,738
(Time to finally zip up the suitcases)

1775
01:16:21,739 --> 01:16:24,532
- Time to pack it all in, right?
- Yeah.

1776
01:16:24,723 --> 01:16:26,048
Let's do this.

1777
01:16:26,482 --> 01:16:28,250
- Let's zip them up.
- And with that...

1778
01:16:28,423 --> 01:16:30,486
- Goodbye!
- Bye!

1779
01:16:32,621 --> 01:16:33,455
Goodbye.

1780
01:16:33,456 --> 01:16:34,590
This is crazy.

1781
01:16:34,591 --> 01:16:37,660
Everyone, you worked so hard.

1782
01:16:37,661 --> 01:16:39,929
- The suitcases went through a lot too.
- See you.

1783
01:16:41,918 --> 01:16:43,532
- Let's lock them up.
- Bye-bye!

1784
01:16:43,533 --> 01:16:45,134
Farewell!

1785
01:16:48,327 --> 01:16:52,273
- Amazing job, everyone.
- Great work, everybody!

1786
01:16:52,808 --> 01:16:54,655
Awesome job, all of you.

1787
01:16:54,656 --> 01:16:56,345
This is wild.

1788
01:16:59,788 --> 01:17:01,951
Am I seriously crying right now?

1789
01:17:02,128 --> 01:17:03,986
Are you for real?

1790
01:17:05,921 --> 01:17:09,581
(The dam finally breaks.)

1791
01:17:09,868 --> 01:17:12,027
Even the production crew is tearing up!

1792
01:17:12,308 --> 01:17:15,053
(Sniffling)

1793
01:17:15,786 --> 01:17:19,866
(A journey that started
with a single suitcase...)

1794
01:17:20,733 --> 01:17:23,766
(finally comes to a close right here.)

1795
01:17:23,767 --> 01:17:25,374
Hug me!

1796
01:17:25,375 --> 01:17:27,576
- Come here!
- Group hug!

1797
01:17:29,162 --> 01:17:30,646
I'll call the slate.

1798
01:17:35,017 --> 01:17:36,085
And cut!

1799
01:17:44,977 --> 01:17:46,617
(Flashing back
to the second packing showdown)

1800
01:17:46,685 --> 01:17:48,397
Does this belong to a dancer?

1801
01:17:48,670 --> 01:17:50,156
Is this Harimu's?

1802
01:17:50,157 --> 01:17:51,783
Busted red-handed!

1803
01:17:51,784 --> 01:17:53,349
Harimu!

1804
01:17:53,350 --> 01:17:55,496
You gave it away way too fast.

1805
01:17:57,244 --> 01:17:59,149
A singer has got to be holding a mic!

1806
01:17:59,150 --> 01:18:01,104
Since you're debuting
as a singer and all...

1807
01:18:01,200 --> 01:18:03,479
<i>BLACKPINK in your area</i>

1808
01:18:03,488 --> 01:18:05,621
(Widening her eyes playfully)

1809
01:18:05,815 --> 01:18:08,294
I've gotten...

1810
01:18:08,295 --> 01:18:09,695
way better now!

1811
01:18:10,168 --> 01:18:12,434
Wait, why are you doing
another 1-on-1 interview right now?

1812
01:18:12,435 --> 01:18:15,445
Think I'll be fully recovered in a week?

1813
01:18:15,452 --> 01:18:16,285
I'll do my best.

1814
01:18:16,286 --> 01:18:17,553
Thank you.

1815
01:18:17,588 --> 01:18:19,689
(Woopsi Tee, Secret Santa gift,
the ring light)

1816
01:18:19,713 --> 01:18:21,686
(Day 1 in Chiang Mai: Reels Night)

1817
01:18:21,973 --> 01:18:23,778
(Bursts into uproarious laughter)

1818
01:18:23,779 --> 01:18:24,972
This should work.

1819
01:18:24,973 --> 01:18:27,273
It's giving queen and royal consort.

1820
01:18:27,553 --> 01:18:28,170
Hop on.

1821
01:18:29,086 --> 01:18:30,732
Harimu is taking the front.

1822
01:18:30,733 --> 01:18:32,107
- Right here?
- Yep.

1823
01:18:32,498 --> 01:18:34,176
I don't think this is happening.
Forget it!

1824
01:18:34,373 --> 01:18:36,566
(Dozens of Reels met their demise
just like this.)

1825
01:18:36,686 --> 01:18:37,469
What about this?

1826
01:18:37,493 --> 01:18:39,312
(Souvenir shopping at Chiang Mai Airport)

1827
01:18:39,313 --> 01:18:43,206
(Meanwhile, Harimu made
a sneaky purchase.)

1828
01:18:43,373 --> 01:18:45,025
(Ta-da!)

1829
01:18:45,026 --> 01:18:48,693
- I'm totally rocking this around.
- Check this out.

1830
01:18:48,913 --> 01:18:51,813
(Secret Santa was far from over.)

1831
01:18:52,759 --> 01:18:55,865
(Trekking through Tumpak Sewu)

1832
01:18:55,866 --> 01:18:57,218
I'm so jealous!

1833
01:18:57,219 --> 01:19:00,353
I wanted to wear cute athletic fits
and shoot content like that too!

1834
01:19:00,626 --> 01:19:02,805
I'm so envious watching
those travel crews.

1835
01:19:02,830 --> 01:19:04,845
I wanted to rock a bikini too!

1836
01:19:04,846 --> 01:19:07,358
If I'd known the vibe was like this,
I would've brought a bikini!

1837
01:19:07,359 --> 01:19:10,412
Listen, I lost so much weight for this!

1838
01:19:12,579 --> 01:19:14,739
(Ipu drew a little something for her.)

1839
01:19:14,926 --> 01:19:15,784
Is this a flower?

1840
01:19:15,809 --> 01:19:17,188
(Nodding)

1841
01:19:17,213 --> 01:19:19,249
Did Ipu just propose to me?

1842
01:19:19,250 --> 01:19:20,656
- It's a flower!
- Yes.

1843
01:19:21,103 --> 01:19:22,343
Ipu!

1844
01:19:22,955 --> 01:19:24,535
Can we snap a photo together?

1845
01:19:26,850 --> 01:19:30,528
- How do you say "thank you" in Korean?
- Gomawo.

1846
01:19:30,649 --> 01:19:31,667
Ttong power?

1847
01:19:32,365 --> 01:19:33,660
- Gomawo.
- Gomawo.

1848
01:19:33,661 --> 01:19:37,920
Then I'll say "gamsahamnida" to you guys.

1849
01:19:37,921 --> 01:19:39,641
(Deeply touched)

1850
01:19:40,047 --> 01:19:43,853
Have you heard of 1G, 2G, 3G, and LTE?

1851
01:19:43,854 --> 01:19:45,087
I'm basically 1G.

1852
01:19:48,075 --> 01:19:49,714
So when are you upgrading to 4G?

1853
01:19:49,715 --> 01:19:52,055
Maybe never.

1854
01:19:53,262 --> 01:19:55,587
I move at my own pace every single day.

1855
01:19:55,588 --> 01:19:56,562
Just so you remember.

1856
01:19:56,702 --> 01:19:58,260
Check the back too.

1857
01:20:00,442 --> 01:20:01,441
Commemorative photo!

1858
01:20:01,442 --> 01:20:02,682
Let's take one!

1859
01:20:03,066 --> 01:20:04,386
Don't forget about me.

1860
01:20:05,731 --> 01:20:08,670
- Don't forget about us, okay?
- Sure.

1861
01:20:09,333 --> 01:20:10,973
Please remember.

1862
01:20:11,942 --> 01:20:15,109
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
